.clientY)))\n              setDraggingBottom(false)\n            }}\n            onPointerCancel={(event) => { abortDrag(() => setDraggingBottom(false), event) }}\n            onLostPointerCapture={() => { abortDrag(() => setDraggingBottom(false)) }}\n          />\n        )}\n        {/*\n          The bottom panel's own close control at its tab strip's right end\n          (the strip reserves the width via CSS so the + menu never hides\n          under it): one tap collapses the panel.\n        */}\n        {!primaryWorkbench && (\n          <Tooltip label={t('collapseBottomPanel')} side=\"bottom\" delayMs={500}>\n            <button\n              type=\"button\"\n              className={css.bottomClose}\n              aria-label={t('collapseBottomPanel')}\n              onClick={() => { store.reduce(toggleBottomPanel) }}\n            >\n              <IconCloseFillRegular size={14} />\n            </button>\n          </Tooltip>\n        )}\n        <div className={css.panelBody}>\n          <Workbench\n            state={state}\n            tree={state.bottomSplits}\n            newTabOptions={newTabOptions}\n            actions={actions}\n            onNewTab={onNewTab}\n            renderTab={renderTab}\n            getTabIcon={tabIconOf}\n            getTabBadge={tabBadgeOf}\n            isTabUnread={isTabUnread}\n            getTabRightActions={tabRightActionsOf}\n            onRevealInFileManager={revealTabFile}\n          />\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n/** The header control that expands/collapses the bottom workbench (see\n *  sidebar/bottom-toggle.tsx — registered into DSH's session header). */\nexport function BottomDockToggle(props: { store: SidebarStore }) {\n  const { store } = props\n  const snapshot = useSyncExternalStore(\n    useCallback((callback: () => void) => store.subscribe(callback), [store]),\n    useCallback(() => store.getSnapshot(), [store]),\n  )\n  // 宿主右侧面板展开时**照常渲染**：本入口在会话头 utilities，位于右栏控件簇\n  // （Split / Fullscreen / Collapse right sidebar）左侧的独立一列，不会被它们盖住。\n  // 早先这里在右栏展开时早退，结果「先开右栏就再也打不开工作台」。\n  const open = snapshot.state?.bottomOpen === true\n  const label = open ? t('collapseBottomPanel') : t('expandBottomPanel')\n  return (\n    <Tooltip label={label} side=\"bottom\" delayMs={500}>\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        className={css.toggleButton}\n        data-dsh-bottom-toggle\n        data-active={open ? 'true' : undefined}\n        aria-label={label}\n        aria-pressed={open}\n        onClick={() => { store.reduce(toggleBottomPanel) }}\n      >\n        <IconPanelBottomOutline16 size={15} />\n      </button>\n    </Tooltip>\n  )\n}\n","/**\n * The plugin's side of a native right-Sidebar tab.\n *\n * A plugin tab descriptor is one registration in the plugin's own registry\n * (`ctx.betterSidebar`); this module adapts the native tab record to that\n * descriptor's component contract. The native surface carries the tab's\n * record (id, kind, title, content identity, navigation params, lifetime\n * signal); the plugin's components expect a `SidebarTab` plus the explorer\n * state the plugin's own layout used to hold — both live here.\n *\n * The adapter owns three things the native layout does not carry:\n *\n * - a synthetic plugin `SidebarTab` per native tab id, minted from the native\n *   record + `navigation.params` and kept live across navigations, so a\n *   component that retitles itself (`updateTab`) or rewrites its path (the\n *   editor's in-place file switch) keeps working;\n * - the explorer's expansion/reveal sets: EXPANSION lives in the per-session\n *   state the workbench already uses (one set per session, shared by every\n *   native tab of that session — a closed tab cannot drop it), while the\n *   transient \"show in folder\" reveal stays per tab;\n * - the per-kind instance counter behind titles like \"Terminal 2\".\n *\n * Nothing here is a singleton: the registry is created once per client\n * activation and handed to every registration.\n */\nimport { createElement, useEffect, useSyncExternalStore } from 'react'\nimport type { TabId, SidebarRightTabActions } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-sidebar-right/client'\nimport type { ComponentType, ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport type { Context } from '../../context-types.ts'\nimport type { SessionScope } from '../api.ts'\nimport { RenderBoundary } from '../RenderBoundary.tsx'\nimport { OrphanedTab } from '../OrphanedTab.tsx'\nimport { ContextDiagnosticsHost } from '../context-diagnostics-ui.tsx'\nimport type { ContextDiagnostics } from '../context-diagnostics.ts'\nimport { referenceInChat } from '../reference-in-chat.ts'\nimport { fileAddressFor } from '../resource-address.ts'\nimport { useSessionRoot } from '../use-session-root.ts'\nimport { useSessionScope } from '../session-scope.ts'\nimport type { BetterSidebarService, NativePathTab } from '../service.ts'\nimport { t } from '../locales.ts'\nimport { isUnread, toggleExpanded } from '../state.ts'\nimport type { SidebarStore, SidebarTab, TabType } from '../state.ts'\nimport css from '../sidebar.module.css'\n\n/** The chip glyph's size: the tab strip's own icon scale. */\nconst CHIP_ICON_SIZE = 14\n\n/** The editor kind: a chip for a file row shows the file's own glyph. */\nconst EDITOR_KIND = 'editor'\n\n/**\n * The plugin-side seed a native open carries in `navigation.params`.\n * JSON-shaped by convention (the native surface does not validate it).\n */\nexport interface NativeTabParams {\n  /** Overrides the descriptor's title for this instance. */\n  readonly title?: string\n  /** A file path (the editor window's content seed). */\n  readonly path?: string\n  /** A URL the tab navigates to on mount (the browser tab's seed). */\n  readonly url?: string\n  /** A diff reference (the diff tab's content seed). */\n  readonly diff?: SidebarTab['diff']\n  /** JSON-serializable custom state carried on the synthetic record. */\n  readonly meta?: unknown\n  /** A line to land on (file addresses carry it as a navigation parameter). */\n  readonly line?: number\n}\n\n/** The native tab information this adapter reads (structural mirror of `useTabInfo`). */\nexport interface NativeTabInfo {\n  readonly tab: {\n    readonly id: TabId\n    readonly kind: string\n    readonly title: string\n    readonly contentId: string\n    readonly visible: boolean\n    readonly navigation: {\n      readonly address: string\n      readonly params: NativeTabParams | undefined\n      readonly revision: number\n    }\n    readonly signal: AbortSignal\n    readonly actions: Pick<SidebarRightTabActions, 'openResource'>\n  }\n}\n\n/** One native tab's plugin-side view state. */\ninterface View {\n  tab: SidebarTab\n  /**\n   * The SEAT session this record belongs to: the session the tab is drawn in,\n   * which is NOT `scope.sessionId` (a file address carries its own content\n   * session, and the two differ whenever a tab shows another session's file).\n   * Recorded rather than re-derived from the view key: `retain()` and\n   * `pathTabs()` both need it, the key encoding is an internal detail, and a\n   * session id may itself contain the separator.\n   */\n  seat: string\n  scope: SessionScope\n  /**\n   * A PROJECTION of the session's expansion set (never an authoritative copy):\n   * refreshed from the store on every `ensure` and on every store change, so\n   * every native tab of one session shows the same set and reopening a tab\n   * cannot reset it. Cached only for referential stability — a fresh array on\n   * each render would re-run the tree's load effect for nothing.\n   */\n  expanded: string[]\n  /** The transient \"show in folder\" highlight: per tab by design. */\n  revealed: string[]\n  /** Bumped on every mutation; the components subscribe to it. */\n  version: number\n}\n\n/**\n * The record key: one native tab id names a tab in EVERY session (the host's\n * per-session counter restarts at `tab1`), and DSH 0.1.7 keeps visited bodies\n * mounted through hiding, tab selection and Session switches\n * (`SidebarRightTabDefinition.keepMounted`). Two sessions' `tab1` are therefore\n * ALIVE AT THE SAME TIME — a registry keyed by the bare id would hand one\n * session's tree/scroll/draft state to the other. The seat's session is part\n * of the record's identity.\n */\nfunction viewKey(sessionId: string, id: string): string {\n  return `${sessionId}::${id}`\n}\n\n/** The plugin-side record registry for native tabs. */\nexport interface NativeTabRecords {\n  /**\n   * The synthetic record for one seat's native tab, minted on first sight and\n   * kept across navigations (a navigation refreshes the seed fields, never the\n   * identity or a plugin-side title/meta mutation).\n   * @param input - the native record, its seat session, and the content scope.\n   * @returns the current view state.\n   */\n  ensure(input: {\n    /**\n     * The SEAT session this tab is drawn in — the record's identity. Not to be\n     * confused with `scope.sessionId`: a file address carries its own session,\n     * which is the namespace its content is read/written in.\n     */\n    sessionId: string\n    id: string\n    kind: string\n    title: string\n    params: NativeTabParams | undefined\n    scope: SessionScope\n    /**\n     * The native navigation revision this call carries. The native surface\n     * re-delivers the LAST navigation on every render (its `useTabInfo`\n     * snapshot is stable until the host really navigates), so the seed `meta`\n     * is adopted once per revision — see {@link createNativeTabRecords}.\n     * Absent (the plugin's own layout, an older caller) never re-adopts.\n     */\n    revision?: number\n    /**\n     * The descriptor's own factory, called ONCE for a record that arrives\n     * without seed fields (a native guide open, which knows nothing about the\n     * plugin's per-instance minting): it supplies the title and the meta a\n     * view needs — the side chat's thread bootstrap, the terminal's name.\n     */\n    mint?: () => { title?: string; meta?: unknown } | undefined\n  }): View\n  /** One record by its seat session and native tab id. */\n  get(sessionId: string, id: string): View | undefined\n  /**\n   * Every record that carries a file path, across every live session. The file\n   * tree's rename/delete reconciliation walks BOTH tab spaces: the bottom\n   * workbench's splits come from the store, and the right column — where files\n   * actually open by default — only exists here. Without this the reconciliation\n   * silently skipped every native editor tab (its next save wrote the OLD name).\n   */\n  pathTabs(): NativePathTab[]\n  /** Whether this seat session has a record for the id. */\n  has(sessionId: string, id: string): boolean\n  /** Merge a patch into the synthetic record (the `updateTab` path). */\n  update(sessionId: string, id: string, patch: { title?: string; path?: string; meta?: unknown }): void\n  /**\n   * Forget one record. Called when the NATIVE TAB really closes — never from a\n   * body unmount, because a Session switch remounts bodies while the reader's\n   * state must survive.\n   */\n  drop(sessionId: string, id: string): void\n  /**\n   * Bind the plugin store — the per-session state is the AUTHORITY for every\n   * view's expansion set. Idempotent; the first call also subscribes to store\n   * changes so a toggle made anywhere (the workbench, another native tab, a\n   * persisted restore) refreshes every native view.\n   */\n  attachStore(store: SidebarStore): void\n  /**\n   * Toggle one directory in the SCOPE session's expansion set (the set every\n   * view of that session mirrors); `sessionId` names the record's SEAT.\n   */\n  toggleExpanded(sessionId: string, id: string, path: string): void\n  /**\n   * Keep only records of these sessions; the rest are forgotten. A session the\n   * user deleted never unmounts anything the plugin can hook, so its records\n   * (and a retained body) would otherwise live for the life of the page.\n   */\n  retain(sessions: ReadonlySet<string>): void\n  /** Mint the next instance number of a kind (titles like \"Terminal 2\"). */\n  nextInstance(kind: string): number\n  /** A per-record version for `useSyncExternalStore`. */\n  versionOf(sessionId: string, id: string): number\n  /** Subscribe to record changes (title/path/meta/expanded). */\n  subscribe(listener: () => void): () => void\n}\n\n/** Whether two expansion sets hold the same paths in the same order. */\nfunction samePaths(left: readonly string[], right: readonly string[]): boolean {\n  return left.length === right.length && left.every((path, index) => path === right[index])\n}\n\n/** Create the record registry for one client activation. */\nexport function createNativeTabRecords(): NativeTabRecords {\n  const views = new Map<string, View>()\n  const instances = new Map<string, number>()\n  /**\n   * Record key -> the navigation revision whose seed meta was last adopted.\n   *\n   * `meta` has two writers: an opener's navigation (a page kind is\n   * re-delivered with fresh `params` on every open — the side chat switches\n   * threads that way) and the view itself through `updateTab` (a tab that\n   * minted a thread binds its id there). The native surface re-delivers the\n   * SAME navigation on every render, so adopting the seed unconditionally\n   * would let the plugin's own write be overwritten on the next pass: the tab\n   * would fall back to \"unbound\" and mint thread after thread. Only a\n   * revision this record has not adopted yet may seed.\n   */\n  const navigationRevisions = new Map<string, number>()\n  const listeners = new Set<() => void>()\n  const notify = (): void => { for (const listener of listeners) listener() }\n  const put = (key: string, view: View): void => {\n    views.set(key, { ...view, version: view.version + 1 })\n    notify()\n  }\n  /** The session-state authority (bound through {@link NativeTabRecords.attachStore}). */\n  let store: SidebarStore | undefined\n  /** The session's expansion set (absent session = nothing expanded yet). */\n  const expandedOf = (sessionId: string): string[] =>\n    store?.getSessionState(sessionId)?.expanded ?? []\n  /**\n   * Re-read every view's expansion projection from the session state. Views\n   * that changed get a version bump (which is what re-renders their bodies);\n   * identical sets keep their array identity so the tree's `expanded` prop —\n   * and therefore its load effect — stays stable.\n   */\n  const syncExpanded = (): void => {\n    if (store === undefined) return\n    let changed = false\n    for (const [id, entry] of views) {\n      // Per-session reads, not one whole-map copy per pass: this runs on EVERY\n      // store notify and the map copy allocated (and invalidated downstream\n      // memos) once per notification.\n      const next = store.getSessionState(entry.scope.sessionId)?.expanded ?? []\n      if (samePaths(entry.expanded, next)) continue\n      views.set(id, { ...entry, expanded: next, version: entry.version + 1 })\n      changed = true\n    }\n    if (changed) notify()\n  }\n  return {\n    attachStore(next) {\n      if (store === next) return\n      store = next\n      // One listener for the whole registry: the store lives as long as this\n      // activation, so the returned disposer is not kept.\n      next.subscribe(syncExpanded)\n      syncExpanded()\n    },\n    ensure({ sessionId, id, kind, title, params, scope, revision, mint }) {\n      const key = viewKey(sessionId, id)\n      const existing = views.get(key)\n      if (existing === undefined) {\n        const seeded = params?.title === undefined && params?.meta === undefined ? mint?.() : undefined\n        const meta = params?.meta ?? seeded?.meta\n        // A url seed lands on `path`: the browser tab reads its address from\n        // there and persists navigations back to the same field, so a record\n        // that dropped it opened with an empty address bar.\n        const path = params?.path ?? params?.url\n        const minted: View = {\n          tab: {\n            id,\n            type: kind as TabType,\n            title: params?.title ?? seeded?.title ?? title,\n            ...(path === undefined ? {} : { path }),\n            ...(params?.line === undefined ? {} : { line: params.line }),\n            ...(params?.diff === undefined ? {} : { diff: params.diff }),\n            ...(meta === undefined ? {} : { meta }),\n          },\n          scope,\n          seat: sessionId,\n          expanded: expandedOf(scope.sessionId),\n          revealed: [],\n          version: 0,\n        }\n        views.set(key, minted)\n        // The seed meta of THIS navigation is what the mint just adopted: a\n        // re-delivery of the same navigation must not re-adopt it (it would\n        // clobber the thread the view writes back through `updateTab`).\n        if (revision !== undefined) navigationRevisions.set(key, revision)\n        return minted\n      }\n      // A navigation may carry new seed fields (the editor's in-place switch,\n      // a browser tab pointed at another URL, a side chat switching threads);\n      // the record's identity and any plugin-side mutation (title from\n      // `updateTab`) stay. `meta` and `path` are the exceptions — both also\n      // have a plugin-side writer, so only a navigation this record has not\n      // adopted yet may seed them (see {@link navigationRevisions}).\n      const patch: Partial<SidebarTab> = {}\n      // Whether the host is addressing this record with a navigation it has not\n      // delivered yet. A revision-less caller (the plugin's own layout, an\n      // older caller) counts as new: it has no ledger to be compared against.\n      const newNavigation = revision === undefined || navigationRevisions.get(key) !== revision\n      if (revision !== undefined && newNavigation) {\n        navigationRevisions.set(key, revision)\n        if (params?.meta !== undefined) patch.meta = params.meta\n      }\n      // `path` rides the same gate as `meta`: the file tree retargets an open\n      // editor onto a renamed file through `updateTab`, and while the host's\n      // address keeps naming the OLD path, honoring it on every render undid\n      // that retarget — the next save wrote a name the user had just renamed\n      // away, recreating it. Only a real navigation (a new revision) may move\n      // the record back onto its address.\n      const nextPath = params?.path ?? params?.url\n      if (nextPath !== undefined && nextPath !== existing.tab.path && newNavigation) {\n        patch.path = nextPath\n      }\n      // The landing line clears as well as sets: an in-place switch from\n      // `a.c:131` to a bare `a.c` must not leave the old line behind and jump\n      // the reader back there. Compared against the current value so the\n      // common case (both absent) adds nothing to the patch and the record\n      // keeps its identity.\n      if (params?.line !== existing.tab.line) patch.line = params?.line\n      if (params?.diff !== undefined) patch.diff = params.diff\n      // The expansion set always mirrors the CURRENT session state (a record\n      // reused for another session must not keep the previous one's set).\n      const expanded = expandedOf(scope.sessionId)\n      if (existing.scope.sessionId !== scope.sessionId || !samePaths(existing.expanded, expanded)) {\n        views.set(key, { ...existing, scope, expanded, tab: { ...existing.tab, ...patch } })\n        return views.get(key)!\n      }\n      if (existing.scope.cwd !== scope.cwd) {\n        views.set(key, { ...existing, scope, tab: { ...existing.tab, ...patch } })\n        return views.get(key)!\n      }\n      if (Object.keys(patch).length === 0) return existing\n      const next: View = { ...existing, tab: { ...existing.tab, ...patch } }\n      views.set(key, next)\n      return next\n    },\n    get: (sessionId, id) => views.get(viewKey(sessionId, id)),\n    pathTabs() {\n      const tabs: NativePathTab[] = []\n      for (const entry of views.values()) {\n        const path = entry.tab.path\n        // A browser tab's address lands on `path` too (a url seed is stored\n        // there), so this is every tab bound to a path or an address.\n        if (path !== undefined) {\n          tabs.push({\n            sessionId: entry.seat,\n            scopeSessionId: entry.scope.sessionId,\n            cwd: entry.scope.cwd,\n            id: entry.tab.id,\n            path,\n            // The chip's title travels with the row: the rename\n            // reconciliation retitles a page only when that title was\n            // derived from the file name (see tree-mutations).\n            title: entry.tab.title,\n          })\n        }\n      }\n      return tabs\n    },\n    has: (sessionId, id) => views.has(viewKey(sessionId, id)),\n    update(sessionId, id, patch) {\n      const key = viewKey(sessionId, id)\n      const entry = views.get(key)\n      if (entry === undefined) return\n      const next: SidebarTab = { ...entry.tab, ...patch }\n      // A path change is a NEW open: the landing line (#826) rides the\n      // navigation that delivered the file, so it must not survive into the\n      // next one — `updateTab` is exactly how an in-place switch and a rename\n      // retarget a record. Keeping it sent the next file to the previous\n      // file's line (and forced a markdown file into the editor).\n      if (patch.path !== undefined && patch.path !== entry.tab.path) next.line = undefined\n      put(key, { ...entry, tab: next })\n    },\n    drop(sessionId, id) {\n      const key = viewKey(sessionId, id)\n      // The revision ledger dies with the record: an id reused later arrives\n      // with its own navigation, and a stale entry would swallow its seed.\n      navigationRevisions.delete(key)\n      if (views.delete(key)) notify()\n    },\n    toggleExpanded(sessionId, id, path) {\n      const entry = views.get(viewKey(sessionId, id))\n      if (entry === undefined || store === undefined) return\n      const scopeSessionId = entry.scope.sessionId\n      // The ACTIVE session goes through `reduce` (it notifies, so the native\n      // views refresh through the subscription); a background session goes\n      // through `reduceFor`, which deliberately stays silent — refresh here.\n      if (store.getSnapshot().sessionId === scopeSessionId) {\n        store.reduce(state => toggleExpanded(state, path))\n        return\n      }\n      store.reduceFor(scopeSessionId, state => toggleExpanded(state, path))\n      syncExpanded()\n    },\n    retain(sessions) {\n      let dropped = false\n      for (const [key, entry] of [...views]) {\n        if (!sessions.has(entry.seat)) {\n          views.delete(key)\n          // The ledger is part of the record (see `drop`): a session the user\n          // deleted must not leave its revisions behind.\n          navigationRevisions.delete(key)\n          dropped = true\n        }\n      }\n      if (dropped) notify()\n    },\n    nextInstance(kind) {\n      const next = (instances.get(kind) ?? 0) + 1\n      instances.set(kind, next)\n      return next\n    },\n    versionOf: (sessionId, id) => views.get(viewKey(sessionId, id))?.version ?? 0,\n    subscribe(listener) {\n      listeners.add(listener)\n      return () => { listeners.delete(listener) }\n    },\n  }\n}\n\n/** What a body registration injects (the plugin's business face). */\nexport interface NativeBodyInjected {\n  readonly sessionId: string\n  readonly ctx: Context\n  readonly store: SidebarStore\n  readonly service: BetterSidebarService\n  readonly records: NativeTabRecords\n  /** The descriptor id this body draws (one registration per descriptor). */\n  readonly descriptorId: string\n  /**\n   * Extra seed fields derived from the native record — a file address carries\n   * its path there, not in `navigation.params`.\n   */\n  readonly paramsOf?: (info: NativeTabInfo) => NativeTabParams | undefined\n  /**\n   * The session the body acts in, when the record names one (a\n   * `session`-scoped file address names its own session); absent falls back to\n   * the session the slot is scoped to.\n   */\n  readonly sessionIdOf?: (info: NativeTabInfo) => string | undefined\n  /**\n   * The activation's optional diagnostics controller (thin wrapper over\n   * ./index.ts's deps): the body below turns it into the provider, because a\n   * native body renders in the HOST's tree and the plugin shell's provider\n   * cannot reach it. Absent = the body renders without diagnostics.\n   */\n  readonly diagnostics?: ContextDiagnostics\n}\n\n/** The props the slot framework adds to every tab body and title. */\nexport interface NativeBodyFrameworkProps {\n  readonly useTabInfo: () => NativeTabInfo\n}\n\n/** Subscribe a component to its own record's mutations. */\nfunction useRecordVersion(records: NativeTabRecords, sessionId: string, id: string): number {\n  return useSyncExternalStore(\n    listener => records.subscribe(listener),\n    () => records.versionOf(sessionId, id),\n  )\n}\n\n/**\n * Open one path through the native tab occurrence that owns the gesture.\n * @param info - the native tab and its Session-bound actions.\n * @param sessionId - the Session whose workspace resolves the path.\n * @param cwd - that Session's workspace root.\n * @param path - an absolute or workspace-relative file path.\n * @param placement - whether the resource reveals a tab, replaces this tab, or opens beside it.\n */\nexport function openNativeFile(\n  info: NativeTabInfo,\n  sessionId: string,\n  cwd: string | undefined,\n  path: string,\n  placement: 'tab' | 'replace' | 'side',\n): void {\n  const options = placement === 'replace' && info.tab.kind !== 'files'\n    ? { replaceTab: true, revealIfOpened: false }\n    : placement === 'side'\n      ? { toSide: true, revealIfOpened: false }\n      : { revealIfOpened: true }\n  info.tab.actions.openResource(fileAddressFor(sessionId, cwd, path), options)\n}\n\n/**\n * One plugin tab rendered inside the native right Sidebar: the descriptor's\n * own component with the plugin's props, over a synthetic record minted from\n * the native tab.\n *\n * The record OUTLIVES this component on purpose. `keepMounted` holds a body\n * mounted through hiding and tab switches, but a Session switch still remounts\n * it on the host side (measured: `drop`+`mint` for the SAME key inside one\n * switch), and the reader's exploration state only lives in the record. The\n * registry therefore keeps it until the tab is closed (`surface.close`) or its\n * session disappears (`retain`) — see the record registry's own notes.\n */\nexport function NativeTabBody(props: NativeBodyInjected & NativeBodyFrameworkProps): ReactNode {\n  const { ctx, store, service, records, descriptorId, useTabInfo } = props\n  const info = useTabInfo()\n  const nativeTab = info.tab\n  // TWO sessions meet here and they are not interchangeable: the SEAT session\n  // (the native column this body is drawn in) keys the record, while the SCOPE\n  // session is the namespace the content is read/written in — a file address\n  // carries its own session, which is the one that resolves its path.\n  const seatSessionId = props.sessionId\n  const scopeSessionId = props.sessionIdOf?.(info) ?? seatSessionId\n  const version = useRecordVersion(records, seatSessionId, nativeTab.id)\n  // A parked body (`visible: false`) must not poll: the host keeps every\n  // visited tab body mounted, so an un-gated 5 s `session.cwd` per body is one\n  // host-side `git` spawn per tab per tick, forever.\n  const cwd = useSessionRoot(ctx, scopeSessionId, { visible: nativeTab.visible })\n  const scope = useSessionScope(scopeSessionId, cwd)\n  // `version` is not read: it only forces this render when the record changed.\n  void version\n  const derived = props.paramsOf?.(info)\n  const params = derived === undefined && nativeTab.navigation.params === undefined\n    ? undefined\n    : { ...derived, ...nativeTab.navigation.params }\n  const descriptor = service.getTab(descriptorId)\n  const view = records.ensure({\n    sessionId: seatSessionId,\n    id: nativeTab.id,\n    kind: nativeTab.kind,\n    title: nativeTab.title,\n    params,\n    scope,\n    revision: nativeTab.navigation.revision,\n    mint: () => {\n      const state = store.getSnapshot().state\n      if (descriptor?.createTab === undefined || state === undefined) return undefined\n      const minted = descriptor.createTab(state)\n      return minted === null ? undefined : { title: minted.tab.title, meta: minted.tab.meta }\n    },\n  })\n  if (descriptor === undefined) {\n    // The orphaned fallback sits in the SAME native host as a live body, so\n    // it gets the same full-height box (its own root also relies on the\n    // `flex: 1` contract the column host restores). The host div carries\n    // `data-dsh-native-tab-host` (empty value) so the e2e lane can assert\n    // the fill, mirroring `data-dsh-better-sidebar`.\n    return createElement(\n      'div',\n      { className: css.nativeTabHost, 'data-dsh-native-tab-host': '' },\n      createElement(OrphanedTab, { ctx, store, scope, tab: view.tab, visible: nativeTab.visible }),\n    )\n  }\n  return createElement(\n    RenderBoundary,\n    { className: css.tabBoundaryError },\n    // The full-height host wrapper (see the `.nativeTabHost` rule in\n    // sidebar.module.css for the native `.paneBody` contract); its\n    // `data-dsh-native-tab-host` attribute lets the e2e lane assert the fill.\n    // The diagnostics provider sits INSIDE the boundary (a body that crashes\n    // must not take the provider's tree with it) and consumes the controller\n    // from this body's own injected bag — the host renders the body, so the\n    // plugin shell's provider is out of reach.\n    createElement(\n      ContextDiagnosticsHost,\n      { controller: props.diagnostics },\n      createElement(\n        'div',\n        { className: css.nativeTabHost, 'data-dsh-native-tab-host': '' },\n        createElement(descriptor.component, {\n          ctx,\n          store,\n          scope,\n          tab: view.tab,\n          visible: nativeTab.visible,\n          expanded: view.expanded,\n          revealed: view.revealed,\n          onToggleDir: (path: string) => { records.toggleExpanded(seatSessionId, nativeTab.id, path) },\n          onReferenceFile: (path: string, isDir: boolean) => { referenceInChat(ctx, scopeSessionId, path, isDir) },\n          onOpenFile: (path: string) => { openNativeFile(info, scopeSessionId, cwd, path, 'tab') },\n          onOpenFileInPlace: (path: string) => { openNativeFile(info, scopeSessionId, cwd, path, 'replace') },\n          onOpenFileSide: (path: string) => { openNativeFile(info, scopeSessionId, cwd, path, 'side') },\n          onOpenDiff: (tab: SidebarTab) => {\n            service.openTab({\n              type: 'diff',\n              title: tab.title,\n              id: tab.id,\n              ...(tab.diff === undefined ? {} : { diff: tab.diff }),\n            }, scope)\n          },\n          onSubagentJump: (childSessionId: string) => {\n            service.openTab({ type: 'subagent', meta: { childSessionId } }, scope)\n          },\n        }),\n      ),\n    ),\n  )\n}\n\n/** What a title registration injects. */\nexport interface NativeTitleInjected {\n  readonly records: NativeTabRecords\n  readonly service: BetterSidebarService\n  /** The descriptor id this title belongs to (one registration per descriptor). */\n  readonly descriptorId: string\n  /**\n   * The seat session this chip is drawn in. The strip renders BEFORE the pane\n   * body, and every session's retitled tabs live in the same registry, so the\n   * chip must name its session instead of reading whichever record the id\n   * happens to hit.\n   */\n  readonly sessionId: string\n  /**\n   * The seed fields the native RECORD itself carries, when the type declares\n   * them (a file address names the file the tab shows).\n   *\n   * The chip must read the file's path from here and not only from\n   * {@link NativeTabRecords}: the plugin-side record is minted by the tab\n   * BODY's render — one commit after the chip first draws — and it is dropped\n   * again when the body unmounts, so a selected file tab used to fall back to\n   * its descriptor's generic glyph every time it was activated.\n   */\n  readonly paramsOf?: (info: NativeTabInfo) => NativeTabParams | undefined\n}\n\n/**\n * A live tab chip: the type's glyph followed by the synthetic record's title\n * (the editor rewrites it on an in-place file switch, the side chat on the\n * thread's first prompt). Without this registration the chip would keep the\n * title captured when the tab opened.\n *\n * The host's tab definition has no icon field — a chip is drawn from the\n * `title` text alone — but this slot IS the chip's content, so the glyph is\n * ours to add. Placement follows the plugin's own semantics: an editor tab\n * with a path shows that file's icon (the same glyph the tree row shows), and\n * every other tab shows its descriptor's icon. Both ride\n * `descriptor.icon`, so the workbench strip, the guide capsules and the chip\n * cannot drift apart.\n */\nexport function NativeTabTitle(props: NativeTitleInjected & NativeBodyFrameworkProps): ReactNode {\n  const { records, service, descriptorId, sessionId, paramsOf, useTabInfo } = props\n  const info = useTabInfo()\n  const nativeTab = info.tab\n  const version = useSyncExternalStore(\n    listener => records.subscribe(listener),\n    () => records.versionOf(sessionId, nativeTab.id),\n  )\n  const record = records.get(sessionId, nativeTab.id)\n  // `version` is read so a title/path/meta mutation re-renders the chip; the\n  // icon itself is derived from the record, never stored.\n  void version\n  const descriptor = service.getTab(descriptorId) ?? service.getTab(record?.tab.type ?? nativeTab.kind)\n  // A single page's title is its type's, read from the registry at render\n  // time: an open tab follows a renamed panel instead of keeping the title\n  // captured when it opened (the record and native tab both store that one).\n  const title = descriptor?.single === true\n    ? (typeof descriptor.title === 'function' ? descriptor.title() : descriptor.title)\n    : record?.tab.title ?? nativeTab.title\n  // The record's own path wins (an in-place switch stores it there, and the\n  // native address of a page kind cannot carry it); the address-derived path\n  // is what keeps the glyph correct when the record is not there YET (the tab\n  // was just activated and the body has not rendered) or has already been\n  // dropped (the body unmounted when the tab was switched away).\n  const path = record?.tab.path ?? paramsOf?.(info)?.path\n  const icon = path !== undefined && descriptorId === EDITOR_KIND\n    ? service.fileIcon(path, CHIP_ICON_SIZE)\n    : undefined\n  const glyph = icon ?? (typeof descriptor?.icon === 'function'\n    ? descriptor.icon(CHIP_ICON_SIZE)\n    : descriptor?.icon)\n  // \"The reader has not looked at this page\": the tab type this chip belongs\n  // to carries a mark (a background activation opened its page without taking\n  // the column over). The unread store subscription is what re-renders the\n  // chip when the mark appears or retires — the native record's own version\n  // does not move for either.\n  const unread = useSyncExternalStore(\n    listener => service.subscribeState(listener),\n    () => isUnread(service.getSnapshot().state, record?.tab.type ?? descriptorId),\n  )\n  // …and the chip is also what RETIRES the mark: this tab being visible means\n  // the reader is looking at its page now. Guarded on BOTH flags, so an\n  // inactive chip (the host draws every expanded tab's title) clears nothing\n  // and a chip with no mark never touches the store.\n  const type = record?.tab.type ?? descriptorId\n  const visible = nativeTab.visible === true\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (visible && unread) service.clearUnread(type, sessionId)\n  }, [visible, unread, type, sessionId, service])\n  if (glyph === undefined || glyph === null) {\n    return unread ? <>{title}<UnreadDot /></> : title\n  }\n  return (\n    <>\n      {/* Decorative: the chip's accessible name stays the title. */}\n      <span className={css.chipIcon} aria-hidden=\"true\">{glyph}</span>\n      {title}\n      {unread ? <UnreadDot /> : null}\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\n/**\n * The native chip's unread mark. `role=\"img\"` + a label so the dot is\n * announced rather than skipped as decoration (the glyph beside it is the\n * decorative one — `aria-hidden` — while this carries the state).\n */\nfunction UnreadDot(): ReactNode {\n  return (\n    <span\n      className={css.chipUnread}\n      role=\"img\"\n      aria-label={t('tabUnread')}\n      title={t('tabUnread')}\n    />\n  )\n}\n\n/** The component pair one descriptor contributes to the native surface. */\nexport interface NativeTabComponents {\n  readonly body: ComponentType<NativeBodyInjected & NativeBodyFrameworkProps>\n  readonly title: ComponentType<NativeTitleInjected & NativeBodyFrameworkProps>\n}\n","/**\n * Identity vocabulary shared by the native tab registration and the start-page\n * takeover. Kept dependency-free so the catalog and the slot registration can\n * both use it without importing each other.\n */\n\n/** The kind the plugin's files window owns (page + file viewer). */\nexport const EDITOR_KIND = 'editor'\n\n/** The built-in page kind this plugin takes over. */\nexport const FILES_KIND = 'files'\n\n/** The prefix of every implementation id this plugin registers natively. */\nconst NATIVE_ID_PREFIX = 'dsh-better-sidebar:'\n\n/** The plugin's implementation id for a descriptor (unique across kinds). */\nexport function nativeId(descriptorId: string): string {\n  return NATIVE_ID_PREFIX + descriptorId\n}\n\n/** Stable identity of one host guide card: provider implementation + entry id. */\nexport function guideKeyOf(providerId: string, entryId: string): string {\n  return providerId + '::' + entryId\n}\n\n/** The native identity a Better Sidebar descriptor registers under. */\nexport function guideIdentityOfDescriptor(descriptorId: string): {\n  providerId: string\n  entryId: string\n  kind: string\n} {\n  if (descriptorId === EDITOR_KIND) {\n    return { providerId: nativeId(FILES_KIND), entryId: FILES_KIND, kind: FILES_KIND }\n  }\n  return { providerId: nativeId(descriptorId), entryId: descriptorId, kind: descriptorId }\n}\n\n/**\n * The Better Sidebar descriptor that owns one native guide card, when it is\n * one of ours. The files takeover is its own registration id but is the\n * editor descriptor's page.\n */\nexport function descriptorIdOfGuideEntry(providerId: string, entryId: string): string | undefined {\n  if (providerId === nativeId(FILES_KIND) && entryId === FILES_KIND) return EDITOR_KIND\n  if (!providerId.startsWith(NATIVE_ID_PREFIX)) return undefined\n  const implementation = providerId.slice(NATIVE_ID_PREFIX.length)\n  return entryId === implementation ? implementation : undefined\n}\n","/**\n * The live inventory of host guide cards (the native start page), as the\n * plugin's own start page and settings section consume it.\n *\n * The host's tab registry is the single authority: a type disabled in the\n * side-card settings unregisters its native type, so its card leaves this\n * catalog too. Entries are kept as thunks/components rather than resolved\n * strings so a language switch re-renders without a registry notification.\n */\nimport type { ComponentType, ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport type { Context } from '../../context-types.ts'\nimport type { TabDescriptor } from '../service.ts'\nimport { descriptorIdOfGuideEntry, guideIdentityOfDescriptor, guideKeyOf } from './guide-ids.ts'\n\n/** One host guide card, normalized for the plugin's own surfaces. */\nexport interface NativeGuideEntry {\n  /** Stable identity: providerId::entryId. */\n  readonly key: string\n  /** Implementation id of the type that contributed the card. */\n  readonly providerId: string\n  /** Entry id inside that provider. */\n  readonly entryId: string\n  /** The kind openTab accepts. */\n  readonly kind: string\n  /** Card title in the active language. */\n  readonly title: () => string\n  /** Optional one-line description in the active language. */\n  readonly description?: () => string\n  /** Optional card glyph component. */\n  readonly icon?: ComponentType<{ size?: number }>\n  /** The Better Sidebar descriptor that owns this card, when it is ours. */\n  readonly descriptorId?: string\n}\n\n/** The catalog face the guide body and the settings section share. */\nexport interface NativeGuideCatalog {\n  /** Reference-stable snapshot of the registered guide cards. */\n  getSnapshot(): readonly NativeGuideEntry[]\n  /** Observe registry changes. */\n  subscribe(listener: () => void): () => void\n}\n\ntype GuideRegistry = Context['sidebarRightTabs']\n\nconst EMPTY: readonly NativeGuideEntry[] = []\n\n/** A descriptor glyph as a component the guide card can render. */\nfunction descriptorIcon(icon: TabDescriptor['icon']): ComponentType<{ size?: number }> | undefined {\n  if (icon === undefined) return undefined\n  if (typeof icon === 'function') {\n    return (props: { size?: number }) => icon(props.size ?? 16)\n  }\n  return () => icon as ReactNode\n}\n\n/** A descriptor's copy, resolved through the same thunk contract as the guide. */\nfunction descriptorTitle(title: TabDescriptor['title']): () => string {\n  return typeof title === 'function' ? title : () => title\n}\n\n/**\n * Merge the live guide cards with every enabled descriptor's synthetic card.\n *\n * A disabled Better Sidebar type unregisters its native type, so it vanishes\n * from the live catalog; the settings/reorder inventory still needs its row so\n * the switch can turn it back on. These synthetic rows never enter the grid\n * (the grid receives the live catalog), only the editable inventory.\n */\nexport function mergeGuideEntries(\n  entries: readonly NativeGuideEntry[],\n  descriptors: readonly TabDescriptor[],\n  tabsEnabled: Readonly<Record<string, boolean>>,\n): NativeGuideEntry[] {\n  const byKey = new Set(entries.map(entry => entry.key))\n  const merged = [...entries]\n  for (const descriptor of descriptors) {\n    if (descriptor.hidden === true || descriptor.bottomOnly === true) continue\n    // An enabled type without a live guide entry simply has no start-page\n    // presence; only a switched-off type needs a synthetic row so its switch\n    // can turn it back on.\n    if (tabsEnabled[descriptor.id] !== false) continue\n    const identity = guideIdentityOfDescriptor(descriptor.id)\n    const key = guideKeyOf(identity.providerId, identity.entryId)\n    if (byKey.has(key)) continue\n    byKey.add(key)\n    const icon = descriptorIcon(descriptor.icon)\n    merged.push({\n      key,\n      providerId: identity.providerId,\n      entryId: identity.entryId,\n      kind: identity.kind,\n      title: descriptorTitle(descriptor.title),\n      ...(descriptor.description === undefined\n        ? {}\n        : { description: typeof descriptor.description === 'function' ? descriptor.description : () => descriptor.description as string }),\n      ...(icon === undefined ? {} : { icon }),\n      descriptorId: descriptor.id,\n    })\n  }\n  return merged\n}\n\n/** One registry snapshot, normalized. */\nfunction entriesOf(registry: GuideRegistry | undefined): readonly NativeGuideEntry[] {\n  if (registry === undefined) return EMPTY\n  return registry.guide().map((entry) => {\n    const descriptorId = descriptorIdOfGuideEntry(entry.providerId, entry.id)\n    return {\n      key: guideKeyOf(entry.providerId, entry.id),\n      providerId: entry.providerId,\n      entryId: entry.id,\n      kind: entry.kind,\n      title: entry.title,\n      ...(entry.description === undefined ? {} : { description: entry.description }),\n      ...(entry.icon === undefined ? {} : { icon: entry.icon }),\n      ...(descriptorId === undefined ? {} : { descriptorId }),\n    }\n  })\n}\n\n/**\n * Create the catalog and wait for the host registry.\n * @param ctx - the client context.\n * @returns the catalog plus the disposer releasing its registry subscription.\n */\nexport function createNativeGuideCatalog(ctx: Context): { catalog: NativeGuideCatalog; dispose: () => void } {\n  const listeners = new Set<() => void>()\n  let snapshot: readonly NativeGuideEntry[] = EMPTY\n  let registry: GuideRegistry | undefined\n  let unsubscribe: (() => void) | undefined\n\n  const publish = (): void => {\n    snapshot = entriesOf(registry)\n    for (const listener of listeners) listener()\n  }\n\n  const seat = ctx.inject(['sidebarRightTabs'], (injected) => {\n    registry = injected.get('sidebarRightTabs')\n    if (registry === undefined) {\n      publish()\n      return\n    }\n    unsubscribe = registry.subscribe(publish)\n    publish()\n    return () => {\n      unsubscribe?.()\n      unsubscribe = undefined\n      registry = undefined\n      publish()\n    }\n  })\n\n  return {\n    catalog: {\n      getSnapshot: () => snapshot,\n      subscribe: (listener) => {\n        listeners.add(listener)\n        return () => { listeners.delete(listener) }\n      },\n    },\n    dispose: () => { void seat.dispose() },\n  }\n}\n","/**\n * Pure start-page layout math: ordering, visibility, the two-column threshold,\n * and the overflow that collapses into the \"More\" card.\n */\n\n/** The wide layout starts at two columns from this pane width on. */\nexport const GUIDE_TWO_COLUMN_MIN_WIDTH = 520\n\n/** Rows a document without a stored value gets. */\nexport const GUIDE_DEFAULT_ROWS = 6\n\n/** One card the layout reasons about. */\nexport interface GuideLayoutEntry {\n  readonly key: string\n}\n\n/** Inputs of computeGuideLayout. */\nexport interface GuideLayoutOptions {\n  /** Explicit start-page order, by card key. */\n  readonly order: readonly string[]\n  /** Visibility overrides; an absent key is visible. */\n  readonly hidden: Readonly<Record<string, boolean>>\n  /** Maximum rows; normalized to at least one. */\n  readonly rows: number\n  /** Pane width in CSS pixels. */\n  readonly width: number\n  /**\n   * Keep one cell for the \"More\" card even when every entry fits. The start\n   * page always offers host actions (browse/create plugins, reorder), so the\n   * card is a persistent affordance rather than overflow-only.\n   */\n  readonly reserveMore?: boolean\n}\n\n/** The settled layout one guide render uses. */\nexport interface GuideLayout<T extends GuideLayoutEntry> {\n  readonly columns: number\n  readonly rows: number\n  readonly capacity: number\n  readonly visible: readonly T[]\n  readonly overflow: readonly T[]\n  readonly showMore: boolean\n}\n\n/** One or two columns for a pane width. */\nexport function columnsForWidth(width: number): number {\n  return width >= GUIDE_TWO_COLUMN_MIN_WIDTH ? 2 : 1\n}\n\n/** Normalize a stored row count; anything below one falls back to the default. */\nexport function normalizeGuideRows(rows: number): number {\n  return Number.isSafeInteger(rows) && rows >= 1 ? rows : GUIDE_DEFAULT_ROWS\n}\n\n/**\n * Sort entries by the stored order. Keys absent from the order follow in their\n * registration order; keys in the order that no longer exist do not matter.\n */\nexport function orderGuideEntries<T extends GuideLayoutEntry>(\n  entries: readonly T[],\n  order: readonly string[],\n): T[] {\n  const rank = new Map<string, number>()\n  for (const [index, key] of order.entries()) if (!rank.has(key)) rank.set(key, index)\n  return entries\n    .map((entry, index) => ({ entry, index, rank: rank.get(entry.key) }))\n    .sort((left, right) => {\n      if (left.rank !== undefined && right.rank !== undefined) {\n        return left.rank - right.rank || left.index - right.index\n      }\n      if (left.rank !== undefined) return -1\n      if (right.rank !== undefined) return 1\n      return left.index - right.index\n    })\n    .map(item => item.entry)\n}\n\n/**\n * Resolve the cards one start page draws.\n *\n * Hidden cards are removed before the capacity check, so hiding a card never\n * creates an artificial overflow. Once the remaining list exceeds the row\n * budget, ONE slot goes to the \"More\" card: visible cards are\n * \"capacity - 1\", and the rest live in its menu. At the minimum capacity of\n * one, the page therefore shows the More card alone.\n */\nexport function computeGuideLayout<T extends GuideLayoutEntry>(\n  entries: readonly T[],\n  options: GuideLayoutOptions,\n): GuideLayout<T> {\n  const rows = normalizeGuideRows(options.rows)\n  const columns = columnsForWidth(options.width)\n  const ordered = orderGuideEntries(entries, options.order)\n  const shown = ordered.filter(entry => options.hidden[entry.key] !== true)\n  const capacity = rows * columns\n  if (options.reserveMore !== true && shown.length <= capacity) {\n    return { columns, rows, capacity, visible: shown, overflow: [], showMore: false }\n  }\n  const visibleCount = Math.max(0, capacity - 1)\n  return {\n    columns,\n    rows,\n    capacity,\n    visible: shown.slice(0, visibleCount),\n    overflow: shown.slice(visibleCount),\n    showMore: true,\n  }\n}\n","/**\n * The shared on/off switch: a real checkbox (native semantics and focus)\n * driving a styled track/thumb. Used by the settings rows and the start-page\n * order list.\n */\nimport css from './Switch.module.css'\n\n/** One labelled switch. */\nexport function Switch(props: {\n  checked: boolean\n  onChange: (next: boolean) => void\n  label: string\n}) {\n  const { checked, onChange, label } = props\n  return (\n    // The parent's write is asynchronous. Derive the next value from the PROP\n    // instead of the event's checkbox state: the controlled value can be reset\n    // before React's change handler runs, which previously made a switch\n    // impossible to turn back on.\n    <label className={css.switch}>\n      <input\n        type=\"checkbox\"\n        className={css.switchInput}\n        checked={checked}\n        aria-label={label}\n        onChange={() => { onChange(!checked) }}\n      />\n      <span className={css.switchTrack} aria-hidden=\"true\">\n        <span className={css.switchThumb} />\n      </span>\n    </label>\n  )\n}\n","/**\n * The maximum-row control shared by the settings section and the guide's\n * reorder dialog. One implementation keeps the clamping and the commit-on-\n * blur/Enter behavior identical in both places.\n */\nimport { Input } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives'\nimport css from './guide.module.css'\n\n/** Props of the shared row-count input. */\nexport interface GuideRowsInputProps {\n  /** The stored maximum row count. */\n  value: number\n  /** Called with a validated count (safe integer >= 1). */\n  onCommit: (rows: number) => void\n  /** Accessible name. */\n  label: string\n}\n\n/** A compact number input that commits on blur or Enter. */\nexport function GuideRowsInput({ value, onCommit, label }: GuideRowsInputProps) {\n  const commit = (raw: string, input: HTMLInputElement): void => {\n    const parsed = Number(raw)\n    const next = Number.isSafeInteger(parsed) && parsed >= 1 ? parsed : value\n    if (next !== value) onCommit(next)\n    input.value = String(next)\n  }\n  return (\n    <Input\n      key={value}\n      type=\"number\"\n      min={1}\n      step={1}\n      className={css.rowsInput}\n      defaultValue={String(value)}\n      aria-label={label}\n      onBlur={event => { commit(event.currentTarget.value, event.currentTarget) }}\n      onKeyDown={(event) => {\n        if (event.key === 'Enter') event.currentTarget.blur()\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}\n","/**\n * Shared start-page order editor: the settings section renders the list inline,\n * the guide's \"More\" menu renders it inside a dialog. Both act on the same\n * catalog/order/visibility vocabulary.\n */\nimport { createElement } from 'react'\nimport {\n  IconChevronDownOutlineRegular,\n  IconChevronUpOutlineRegular,\n  Modal,\n} from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives'\nimport clsx from 'clsx'\nimport type { NativeGuideEntry } from './guide-catalog.ts'\nimport { t } from '../locales.ts'\nimport { Switch } from '../Switch.tsx'\nimport { GuideRowsInput } from './guide-rows.tsx'\nimport css from './guide.module.css'\n\n/** The list's actions; callers own persistence. */\nexport interface GuideOrderListProps {\n  entries: readonly NativeGuideEntry[]\n  hidden: Readonly<Record<string, boolean>>\n  onMove: (key: string, delta: -1 | 1) => void\n  onToggle: (entry: NativeGuideEntry, hidden: boolean) => void\n}\n\n/** The inline order/visibility list. */\nexport function GuideOrderList({ entries, hidden, onMove, onToggle }: GuideOrderListProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className={css.orderList}>\n      {entries.map((entry, index) => {\n        const shown = hidden[entry.key] !== true\n        const title = entry.title()\n        const description = entry.description?.() ?? entry.kind\n        return (\n          <div className={clsx(css.orderRow, !shown && css.orderRowHidden)} key={entry.key}>\n            <span className={css.orderIcon} aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              {entry.icon === undefined ? null : createElement(entry.icon, { size: 16 })}\n            </span>\n            <span className={css.orderText}>\n              <span className={css.orderTitle}>{title}</span>\n              <span className={css.orderDesc}>{description}</span>\n            </span>\n            <span className={css.orderActions}>\n              <button\n                type=\"button\"\n                className={css.orderButton}\n                aria-label={`${t('guideOrder')}: ${title} ↑`}\n                disabled={index === 0}\n                onClick={() => { onMove(entry.key, -1) }}\n              >\n                <IconChevronUpOutlineRegular size={12} />\n              </button>\n              <button\n                type=\"button\"\n                className={css.orderButton}\n                aria-label={`${t('guideOrder')}: ${title} ↓`}\n                disabled={index === entries.length - 1}\n                onClick={() => { onMove(entry.key, 1) }}\n              >\n                <IconChevronDownOutlineRegular size={12} />\n              </button>\n              <Switch\n                label={`${entry.descriptorId === undefined ? t('settingsGuideShow') : t('settingsGuideEnable')}: ${title}`}\n                checked={shown}\n                onChange={(next) => { onToggle(entry, !next) }}\n              />\n            </span>\n          </div>\n        )\n      })}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n/** The order editor opened from the guide's \"More\" menu. */\nexport function GuideOrderDialog(props: GuideOrderListProps & {\n  open: boolean\n  onClose: () => void\n  rows: number\n  onRows: (rows: number) => void\n}) {\n  const { open, onClose, entries, hidden, onMove, onToggle, rows, onRows } = props\n  return (\n    <Modal\n      open={open}\n      onClose={onClose}\n      title={t('guideOrder')}\n      closeLabel={t('dismiss')}\n      footer={(\n        <button type=\"button\" className={css.dialogDone} onClick={onClose}>\n          {t('settingsDone')}\n        </button>\n      )}\n    >\n      <div className={css.dialogRow}>\n        <span className={css.dialogRowText}>\n          <span className={css.dialogRowTitle}>{t('settingsGuideRowsTitle')}</span>\n          <span className={css.dialogRowDesc}>{t('settingsGuideRowsDesc')}</span>\n        </span>\n        <GuideRowsInput\n          value={rows}\n          label={t('settingsGuideRowsTitle')}\n          onCommit={onRows}\n        />\n      </div>\n      <GuideOrderList entries={entries} hidden={hidden} onMove={onMove} onToggle={onToggle} />\n    </Modal>\n  )\n}\n","/**\n * Serialized writes for the start page's own preferences from the guide card's\n * \"Reorder\" dialog. The settings section has its own revision-guarded queue;\n * this one uses the same revision-free settings route as the editor's\n * plugin-owned settings, and adopts the returned document.\n */\nimport { api } from '../api.ts'\nimport { parsePrefs } from '../prefs.ts'\nimport type { SidebarStore } from '../state.ts'\n\nlet queue: Promise<void> = Promise.resolve()\n\n/** Persist one patch of start-page preferences. */\nexport function writeGuidePrefs(store: SidebarStore, patch: Record<string, unknown>): void {\n  queue = queue.then(async () => {\n    const view = await api.settingsUpdate(patch)\n    store.setPrefs(parsePrefs(view.value))\n  }).catch((error: unknown) => {\n    console.error('start page settings write failed', error)\n  })\n}\n\n/** Persist the full explicit order. */\nexport function saveGuideOrder(store: SidebarStore, order: readonly string[]): void {\n  writeGuidePrefs(store, { guideOrder: [...order] })\n}\n\n/** Persist one card's start-page visibility. */\nexport function setGuideEntryHidden(store: SidebarStore, key: string, hidden: boolean): void {\n  const current = store.getPrefs().guideHidden\n  const next = { ...current }\n  if (hidden) next[key] = true\n  else delete next[key]\n  writeGuidePrefs(store, { guideHidden: next })\n}\n\n/** Persist one Better Sidebar type's feature switch (the sidebar-content state). */\nexport function setGuideEntryEnabled(store: SidebarStore, descriptorId: string, enabled: boolean): void {\n  const current = store.getPrefs().tabsEnabled\n  writeGuidePrefs(store, { tabsEnabled: { ...current, [descriptorId]: enabled } })\n}\n\n/** Persist the maximum row count. */\nexport function saveGuideRows(store: SidebarStore, rows: number): void {\n  writeGuidePrefs(store, { guideRows: rows })\n}\n","/**\n * The plugin's start page: the native guide slot's chain replacement.\n *\n * It draws the host's registered guide cards itself so the page can use a\n * two-column grid, a configurable row budget, and a \"More\" card. A card is\n * opened through the guide tab's own actions, exactly like the shipped guide\n * does, so the guide tab is replaced rather than left behind.\n */\nimport { createElement, useEffect, useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState, useSyncExternalStore } from 'react'\nimport type { ComponentType, ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport {\n  IconEllipsisOutlineRegular,\n  IconPluginPinwheelOutlineRegular,\n  IconPlusOutlineRegular,\n  IconSettingsOutlineRegular,\n  Menu,\n} from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives'\nimport clsx from 'clsx'\nimport type { SidebarPrefs } from '../../prefs-shared.ts'\nimport type { HostShellCatalog } from '../terminal-client.ts'\nimport type { SidebarStore } from '../state.ts'\nimport type { BetterSidebarService } from '../service.ts'\nimport { t } from '../locales.ts'\nimport { mergeGuideEntries, type NativeGuideCatalog, type NativeGuideEntry } from './guide-catalog.ts'\nimport { columnsForWidth, computeGuideLayout, orderGuideEntries } from './guide-layout.ts'\nimport { GuideOrderDialog } from './guide-order.tsx'\nimport { saveGuideOrder, saveGuideRows, setGuideEntryEnabled, setGuideEntryHidden } from './guide-prefs.ts'\nimport css from './guide.module.css'\n\n/** The terminal service slice the card's native menu needs. */\nexport interface GuideShellMenu {\n  launchShells: (signal: AbortSignal) => Promise<HostShellCatalog>\n  selectShell: (path: string) => void\n}\n\n/** The native tab actions a guide card opens through (structurally the host's). */\ninterface GuideActions {\n  openTab: (kind: string, options: { replaceTab?: boolean; params?: Record<string, unknown> }) => void\n  close: () => void\n}\n\n/** What the chain component receives from the native registration. */\nexport interface NativeGuideProps {\n  /** Host-injected hook for the guide tab's own record. */\n  useTabInfo?: () => { tab: { actions: GuideActions } } | undefined\n  catalog: NativeGuideCatalog\n  store: SidebarStore\n  /** The plugin registry, so disabled types stay in the reorder inventory. */\n  service: BetterSidebarService\n  /** Present only when the host exposes both shell catalog and selection. */\n  shellMenu?: GuideShellMenu | undefined\n  /** Host plugin discovery action, when the service exists. */\n  onBrowsePlugins?: () => void\n  /** Host \"create your plugin\" action, when the workspace can start a session. */\n  onCreatePlugin?: () => void\n}\n\n/** The grid's inputs, extracted for direct rendering in tests. */\nexport interface GuideGridProps {\n  entries: readonly NativeGuideEntry[]\n  prefs: Pick<SidebarPrefs, 'guideOrder' | 'guideHidden' | 'guideRows' | 'guideAlign' | 'tabsEnabled'>\n  /** Pane width in CSS pixels. */\n  width: number\n  onOpen: (entry: NativeGuideEntry, params?: Record<string, unknown>) => void\n  onSaveOrder?: (order: readonly string[]) => void\n  onToggleHidden?: (entry: NativeGuideEntry, hidden: boolean) => void\n  onSaveRows?: (rows: number) => void\n  /** The editable inventory (live cards plus disabled plugin descriptors). */\n  inventory?: readonly NativeGuideEntry[]\n  /** Host \"Browse other plugins\" action, when the navigation service exists. */\n  onBrowsePlugins?: () => void\n  /** Host \"Create your plugin\" action, when the workspace can start a session. */\n  onCreatePlugin?: () => void\n  shellMenu?: GuideShellMenu | undefined\n}\n\n/** One card's glyph, when it has one. */\nfunction cardIcon(entry: NativeGuideEntry): ReactNode {\n  const Icon: ComponentType<{ size?: number }> | undefined = entry.icon\n  return Icon === undefined ? null : createElement(Icon, { size: 16 })\n}\n\n/** Menu glyphs sit in a fixed 14px box; some custom icons keep their own\n *  baseline, so center the SVG explicitly or it rides 2px above the label. */\nfunction menuIcon(icon: ReactNode): ReactNode {\n  return icon === null ? null : <span className={css.menuIcon} aria-hidden=\"true\">{icon}</span>\n}\n\n/** The terminal card's shell menu: the host's shell catalog, drawn natively here. */\nfunction TerminalMenu(props: {\n  entry: NativeGuideEntry\n  shellMenu: GuideShellMenu\n  onOpen: (entry: NativeGuideEntry, params?: Record<string, unknown>) => void\n}) {\n  const { entry, shellMenu, onOpen } = props\n  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)\n  const [attempt, setAttempt] = useState(0)\n  const [state, setState] = useState<\n    | { phase: 'loading' }\n    | { phase: 'ready'; shells: HostShellCatalog['shells']; selected?: string }\n    | { phase: 'failed'; message: string }\n  >({ phase: 'loading' })\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!open) return\n    const lifetime = new AbortController()\n    let live = true\n    setState({ phase: 'loading' })\n    Promise.resolve()\n      .then(() => shellMenu.launchShells(lifetime.signal))\n      .then((catalog) => {\n        if (!live) return\n        setState({\n          phase: 'ready',\n          shells: catalog.shells,\n          ...(catalog.selectedShell === undefined ? {} : { selected: catalog.selectedShell }),\n        })\n      }, (error: unknown) => {\n        if (!live) return\n        setState({ phase: 'failed', message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error) })\n      })\n    return () => {\n      live = false\n      lifetime.abort()\n    }\n  }, [open, attempt, shellMenu])\n\n  const items = state.phase === 'loading'\n    ? [{ id: 'loading', label: t('loading'), disabled: true }]\n    : state.phase === 'failed'\n      ? [\n        { id: 'failed', label: t('guideShellFailed', { error: state.message }), disabled: true },\n        { id: 'retry', label: t('terminalRetry') },\n      ]\n      : state.shells.length === 0\n        ? [{ id: 'empty', label: t('guideShellEmpty'), disabled: true }]\n        : state.shells.map(shell => ({ id: shell.path, label: shell.name }))\n\n  return (\n    <Menu\n      open={open}\n      onClose={() => { setOpen(false) }}\n      portal\n      autoFocus\n      align=\"end\"\n      items={items}\n      selectedId={state.phase === 'ready' ? state.selected : undefined}\n      onSelect={(id) => {\n        if (state.phase === 'failed') {\n          if (id === 'retry') setAttempt(value => value + 1)\n          return\n        }\n        if (state.phase !== 'ready') return\n        shellMenu.selectShell(id)\n        setOpen(false)\n        onOpen(entry, { shellPath: id })\n      }}\n      anchor={(\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className={css.cardMenuButton}\n          data-guide-shell-menu=\"true\"\n          aria-label={t('terminal')}\n          aria-haspopup=\"menu\"\n          aria-expanded={open}\n          onClick={() => { setOpen(value => !value) }}\n        >\n          <IconEllipsisOutlineRegular size={14} />\n        </button>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}\n\n/** One card in the start-page grid. */\nfunction GuideCard(props: {\n  entry: NativeGuideEntry\n  onOpen: (entry: NativeGuideEntry, params?: Record<string, unknown>) => void\n  shellMenu?: GuideShellMenu | undefined\n}) {\n  const { entry, onOpen, shellMenu } = props\n  const description = entry.description?.()\n  const terminal = entry.kind === 'terminal' && shellMenu !== undefined\n  return (\n    <div className={css.card} data-sidebar-right-guide-entry={entry.kind}>\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        className={css.cardMain}\n        aria-label={description === undefined ? entry.title() : entry.title() + ' ' + description}\n        onClick={() => { onOpen(entry) }}\n      >\n        <span className={css.cardIcon} aria-hidden=\"true\">{cardIcon(entry)}</span>\n        <span className={css.cardText}>\n          <span className={css.cardTitle}>{entry.title()}</span>\n          {description === undefined ? null : <span className={css.cardDesc}>{description}</span>}\n        </span>\n      </button>\n      {terminal ? <TerminalMenu entry={entry} shellMenu={shellMenu} onOpen={onOpen} /> : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n/** The whole start-page grid, including the More card and the order dialog. */\nexport function GuideGrid(props: GuideGridProps) {\n  const {\n    entries, prefs, width, onOpen, onSaveOrder, onToggleHidden, onSaveRows,\n    onBrowsePlugins, onCreatePlugin, shellMenu,\n  } = props\n  const inventory = props.inventory ?? entries\n  const [orderOpen, setOrderOpen] = useState(false)\n  const [moreOpen, setMoreOpen] = useState(false)\n  // A Better Sidebar type's switch is the FEATURE switch (tabsEnabled), not\n  // the start-page visibility map; older guideHidden keys for those types are\n  // ignored so the two surfaces cannot disagree.\n  const hiddenForLayout: Record<string, boolean> = { ...prefs.guideHidden }\n  for (const entry of entries) {\n    if (entry.descriptorId !== undefined) delete hiddenForLayout[entry.key]\n  }\n  const layout = computeGuideLayout(entries, {\n    order: prefs.guideOrder,\n    hidden: hiddenForLayout,\n    rows: prefs.guideRows,\n    width,\n    // The More card is also the home of the host's plugin discovery/creation\n    // actions, so it stays available even when every tab fits.\n    reserveMore: true,\n  })\n  const orderedAll = orderGuideEntries(inventory, prefs.guideOrder)\n  const switchHidden: Record<string, boolean> = {}\n  for (const entry of orderedAll) {\n    switchHidden[entry.key] = entry.descriptorId === undefined\n      ? prefs.guideHidden[entry.key] === true\n      : prefs.tabsEnabled[entry.descriptorId] === false\n  }\n\n  const move = (key: string, delta: -1 | 1): void => {\n    const keys = orderedAll.map(entry => entry.key)\n    const at = keys.indexOf(key)\n    const to = at + delta\n    if (at < 0 || to < 0 || to >= keys.length) return\n    const next = [...keys]\n    const [moved] = next.splice(at, 1)\n    if (moved === undefined) return\n    next.splice(to, 0, moved)\n    onSaveOrder?.(next)\n  }\n\n  const hostActions = [\n    ...(onBrowsePlugins === undefined\n      ? []\n      : [{ id: 'browse', label: t('guideBrowsePlugins'), icon: menuIcon(<IconPluginPinwheelOutlineRegular size={16} />) }]),\n    ...(onCreatePlugin === undefined\n      ? []\n      : [{ id: 'create', label: t('guideCreatePlugin'), icon: menuIcon(<IconPlusOutlineRegular size={16} />) }]),\n  ]\n  const moreItems = [\n    ...layout.overflow.map(entry => ({\n      id: 'open:' + entry.key,\n      label: entry.title(),\n      icon: menuIcon(cardIcon(entry)),\n    })),\n    ...(layout.overflow.length === 0 ? [] : [{ type: 'separator' as const, id: 'overflow-separator' }]),\n    ...hostActions,\n    ...(hostActions.length === 0 ? [] : [{ type: 'separator' as const, id: 'actions-separator' }]),\n    { id: 'order', label: t('guideOrder'), icon: menuIcon(<IconSettingsOutlineRegular size={14} />) },\n  ]\n\n  /** The grid body; the More anchor is a card-sized Menu trigger. */\n  const moreCard = (\n    <div className={css.moreSlot}>\n    <Menu\n      open={moreOpen}\n      onClose={() => { setMoreOpen(false) }}\n      portal\n      autoFocus\n      align=\"end\"\n      items={moreItems}\n      onSelect={(id) => {\n        setMoreOpen(false)\n        if (id === 'browse') {\n          onBrowsePlugins?.()\n          return\n        }\n        if (id === 'create') {\n          onCreatePlugin?.()\n          return\n        }\n        if (id === 'order') {\n          setOrderOpen(true)\n          return\n        }\n        if (!id.startsWith('open:')) return\n        const key = id.slice('open:'.length)\n        const entry = layout.overflow.find(candidate => candidate.key === key)\n        if (entry !== undefined) onOpen(entry)\n      }}\n      anchor={(\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className={clsx(css.card, css.moreCard)}\n          data-guide-more=\"true\"\n          aria-label={t('guideMore')}\n          aria-haspopup=\"menu\"\n          aria-expanded={moreOpen}\n          onClick={() => { setMoreOpen(value => !value) }}\n        >\n          <span className={css.cardIcon} aria-hidden=\"true\">\n            <IconEllipsisOutlineRegular size={18} />\n          </span>\n          <span className={css.cardText}>\n            <span className={css.cardTitle}>{t('guideMore')}</span>\n          </span>\n        </button>\n      )}\n    />\n    </div>\n  )\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      className={css.guide}\n      data-guide-columns={layout.columns}\n      data-guide-rows={layout.rows}\n      data-guide-align={prefs.guideAlign}\n    >\n      {layout.visible.length === 0 && !layout.showMore ? (\n        <p className={css.empty}>{t('guideEmpty')}</p>\n      ) : (\n        <div className={clsx(css.grid, layout.columns === 2 ? css.gridTwo : css.gridOne)}>\n          {layout.visible.map(entry => (\n            <GuideCard key={entry.key} entry={entry} onOpen={onOpen} shellMenu={shellMenu} />\n          ))}\n          {layout.showMore ? moreCard : null}\n        </div>\n      )}\n      <GuideOrderDialog\n        open={orderOpen}\n        onClose={() => { setOrderOpen(false) }}\n        entries={orderedAll}\n        hidden={switchHidden}\n        onMove={move}\n        onToggle={(entry, hidden) => { onToggleHidden?.(entry, hidden) }}\n        rows={prefs.guideRows}\n        onRows={(next) => { onSaveRows?.(next) }}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n/** Measure the pane width so the grid can choose one or two columns. */\nfunction useGuideWidth(ref: { current: HTMLDivElement | null }): number {\n  const [width, setWidth] = useState(0)\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const node = ref.current\n    if (node === null) return\n    const measure = (): void => { setWidth(node.clientWidth) }\n    measure()\n    if (typeof ResizeObserver === 'undefined') return\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(measure)\n    observer.observe(node)\n    return () => { observer.disconnect() }\n  }, [ref])\n  return width\n}\n\n/** The chain component registered into the host's guide slot. */\nexport function NativeGuide(props: NativeGuideProps) {\n  const { catalog, store, service, shellMenu, onBrowsePlugins, onCreatePlugin, useTabInfo } = props\n  const entries = useSyncExternalStore(catalog.subscribe, catalog.getSnapshot, catalog.getSnapshot)\n  const [descriptors, setDescriptors] = useState(() => service.getTabs())\n  useEffect(() => service.subscribe(() => setDescriptors(service.getTabs())), [service])\n  // The store's members are methods (they read their receiver); bind them\n  // through arrows or useSyncExternalStore crashes on the first render.\n  const snapshot = useSyncExternalStore(\n    (listener) => store.subscribe(listener),\n    () => store.getSnapshot(),\n    () => store.getSnapshot(),\n  )\n  const prefs = snapshot.prefs\n  const liveEntries = entries.filter(entry => entry.descriptorId === undefined\n    || prefs.tabsEnabled[entry.descriptorId] !== false)\n  const inventory = mergeGuideEntries(entries, descriptors, prefs.tabsEnabled)\n  const rootRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null)\n  const width = useGuideWidth(rootRef)\n  const actions = useTabInfo?.()?.tab.actions\n\n  const open = (entry: NativeGuideEntry, params?: Record<string, unknown>): void => {\n    if (actions === undefined) return\n    actions.openTab(entry.kind, { replaceTab: true, ...(params === undefined ? {} : { params }) })\n    actions.close()\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      ref={rootRef}\n      className={clsx(css.root, prefs.guideAlign === 'top' ? css.rootTop : css.rootCenter)}\n      data-sidebar-right-guide=\"\"\n      data-dsh-guide-grid=\"true\"\n      data-guide-columns={columnsForWidth(width)}\n      data-guide-rows={prefs.guideRows}\n      data-guide-align={prefs.guideAlign}\n    >\n      <GuideGrid\n        entries={liveEntries}\n        inventory={inventory}\n        prefs={prefs}\n        width={width}\n        onOpen={open}\n        onSaveOrder={(order) => { saveGuideOrder(store, order) }}\n        onToggleHidden={(entry, hidden) => {\n          if (entry.descriptorId === undefined) setGuideEntryHidden(store, entry.key, hidden)\n          else setGuideEntryEnabled(store, entry.descriptorId, !hidden)\n        }}\n        onSaveRows={(next) => { saveGuideRows(store, next) }}\n        onBrowsePlugins={onBrowsePlugins}\n        onCreatePlugin={onCreatePlugin}\n        shellMenu={shellMenu}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n","import type { SessionId } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-session/types'\n/**\n * The plugin's content, registered into DSH's native right Sidebar.\n *\n * Every tab the plugin can draw becomes a native tab TYPE plus a BODY:\n *\n * - the `editor` type is both a page (the files window) and a resource\n *   viewer — it claims `dsh-resource://file/**` at the default `extension`\n *   band, which outranks the built-in `text` preview (`fallback`), so a file\n *   the product opens lands in the plugin's editor — EXCEPT the formats\n *   {@link hostOwnedPath} hands back to DSH's own previews, which are\n *   strictly better for binary documents (host-side Office→PDF conversion,\n *   a worker-backed spreadsheet table, a zoom viewport);\n * - the built-in `files` page kind is TAKEN OVER by an `extension`\n *   registration of the same kind, so `openTab('files')` draws the plugin's\n *   explorer instead of the built-in tree; the built-in resumes when this\n *   plugin unregisters;\n * - every descriptor not marked workbench-only (changes / subagent / side chat /\n *   browser / diff) becomes a page type of its own.\n *\n * The registrations follow the plugin's registry lifecycle: a descriptor\n * registered later (an external plugin) gets its native type too, and a type\n * the user disabled in the side-card settings is unregistered — so it is\n * absent from the native guide and `openTab` refuses it.\n */\nimport type { ISidebarRight, SidebarRightCloseHandler, SidebarRightGuideEntry } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-sidebar-right/client'\nimport type {} from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace/client'\nimport type {} from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-plugin-manager/client'\nimport type { Context } from '../../context-types.ts'\nimport { addressBaseOf, resolveAddressPath } from '../address-base.ts'\nimport { flushDraftBackups } from '../editor-draft-backup.ts'\nimport { t } from '../locales.ts'\nimport { splitTrailingLineSpec } from '../path-line.ts'\nimport { baseName } from '../paths.ts'\nimport { parseFileAddress } from '../resource-address.ts'\nimport { isNativeDocumentPath } from './file-types.ts'\nimport type { ContextDiagnostics } from '../context-diagnostics.ts'\nimport type { BetterSidebarService, TabDescriptor } from '../service.ts'\nimport type { SidebarStore } from '../state.ts'\nimport { webTerminals } from '../terminal-client.ts'\nimport type { NativeGuideCatalog } from './guide-catalog.ts'\nimport { NativeGuide } from './guide.tsx'\nimport { EDITOR_KIND, FILES_KIND, nativeId } from './guide-ids.ts'\nimport { mountedSessionId } from './surface.ts'\nimport {\n  NativeTabBody,\n  NativeTabTitle,\n  type NativeBodyInjected,\n  type NativeTabInfo,\n  type NativeTabParams,\n  type NativeTabRecords,\n} from './tab-adapter.tsx'\n\n/**\n * Additional extensions DSH's own previews own, besides the PDF and Office files\n * shared with the workbench through {@link isNativeDocumentPath}.\n *\n * DSH 0.1.7 grew a real document-preview package (host-side Office→PDF\n * conversion, a worker-backed spreadsheet table, image/PDF zoom viewports and\n * per-directory auto-refresh) for exactly these formats, while the plugin's\n * equivalents are read-only fallbacks. The plugin keeps what the built-in does\n * NOT do: Markdown through its own renderer, HTML through its sandboxed route\n * with the `htmlViewerNoSandbox` safety valve, and — through the `code`\n * catch-all — a genuinely EDITABLE CodeMirror buffer for every text file.\n *\n * Refusing here is what hands the address over: `canOpen` returning false\n * leaves the built-in `text` type (the `fallback` band) as the only claimant.\n *\n * Together these are exactly the set the host renders — nothing more. Nine extensions\n * that the host has NO renderer for (`xlsb xlt xltx xltm ots dot dotx avif`)\n * used to be refused here too, and refusing them turned \"the plugin shows a\n * download panel\" into \"the host shows 'preview is not available for this file\n * type yet'\" — a dead end. They are claimed again, so the `code` catch-all\n * takes them to the binary download pane. `fods` stays refused on purpose: the\n * host's plain-text fallback renders flat ODS XML, which beats a download.\n * `tests/native-surface.spec.ts` pins both directions of this boundary.\n */\nconst HOST_OWNED_EXTS: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set([\n  // Spreadsheets: the built-in renders a table in a worker.\n  'csv', 'tsv', 'fods',\n  // Images: the built-in viewer adds a zoom viewport.\n  'png', 'jpg', 'jpeg', 'gif', 'webp', 'svg', 'bmp', 'ico',\n])\n\n/**\n * Whether DSH's own preview owns one path.\n * @param path - the address's decoded path.\n * @returns true for a shipped host preview extension (a dotfile is not one).\n */\nfunction hostOwnedPath(path: string): boolean {\n  if (isNativeDocumentPath(path)) return true\n  const name = path.slice(path.lastIndexOf('/') + 1)\n  const dot = name.lastIndexOf('.')\n  return dot > 0 && HOST_OWNED_EXTS.has(name.slice(dot + 1).toLowerCase())\n}\n\n/** Tab descriptors eligible for the native right Sidebar. */\nexport function nativeTabDescriptors(service: BetterSidebarService): readonly TabDescriptor[] {\n  return service.getTabs().filter(descriptor => descriptor.native !== false && descriptor.bottomOnly !== true && service.isTabEnabled(descriptor.id))\n}\n\n/** The descriptor's title text, evaluated fresh for the current locale. */\nfunction titleOf(descriptor: TabDescriptor): string {\n  return typeof descriptor.title === 'function' ? descriptor.title() : descriptor.title\n}\n\n/**\n * The guide fields carrying the descriptor's own description line, evaluated\n * fresh for the current locale. DSH 0.1.5-rc.1+ renders `description` only\n * while the guide lists at most 4 entries, and a descriptor that declares\n * none must reach the host with NO `description` field at all — the host has\n * no fallback of its own, so an empty string would render as a blank second\n * line rather than a clean title-only capsule.\n * @param descriptor - the tab descriptor owning the guide entry.\n * @returns the `description` field, or an empty object.\n */\nfunction guideDescriptionOf(descriptor: TabDescriptor | undefined): { description?: () => string } {\n  const description = descriptor?.description\n  return description === undefined ? {} : { description: () => (typeof description === 'function' ? description() : description) }\n}\n\n/**\n * The guide row's glyph for a descriptor icon (nothing when it has none).\n * The native guide renders `entry.icon`, so a takeover registered without one\n * is the only row in the list with a blank leading slot.\n * @param icon - the descriptor's icon value.\n * @returns the guide-entry icon fields, or an empty object.\n */\nfunction guideIconOf(icon: TabDescriptor['icon']): Pick<SidebarRightGuideEntry, 'icon'> {\n  return typeof icon === 'function' ? { icon: props => icon(props.size ?? 16) } : {}\n}\n\n/**\n * The chip title of a file address: its own file name. A resource tab is\n * identified by its address, so the strip must name the FILE — the\n * descriptor's title (\"Files\") would make every open file look identical.\n * @param address - the native tab's content address.\n * @returns the file name, or undefined when the address is not a file.\n */\nfunction fileTitleOf(address: string): string | undefined {\n  const parsed = parseFileAddress(address)\n  if (parsed === undefined) return undefined\n  // A `path:line` spec DSH's markdown grammar left in the address names a\n  // LINE, not a file: the tab is titled after the file (#826).\n  const path = splitTrailingLineSpec(parsed.path)?.path ?? parsed.path\n  const segments = path.split('/').filter(segment => segment !== '')\n  return segments.length === 0 ? undefined : segments[segments.length - 1]\n}\n\n/** One descriptor's live native registrations. */\ninterface Registration {\n  readonly dispose: () => void\n}\n\n/**\n * The plugin-side seed a file-address tab carries.\n *\n * The path comes from the address, and that is also where a `path:line` spec\n * the host's markdown grammar left in it has to come off: DSH reads a `#`-less\n * destination as the file name verbatim, so `[a/b.c](a/b.c:131)` addresses a\n * file called `b.c:131` and the editor reports it missing (#826). The tab\n * TITLE is seeded from the same spec, because the host derives it from the same\n * string and would otherwise label the tab `b.c:131`.\n *\n * The LINE rides along in the same seed. DSH's own `#L131` form already\n * arrives as `navigation.params.line` (the host parses it and sends it down),\n * so seeding it here is what makes both spellings land on the same row — see\n * {@link NativeTabParams.line}. The range end and the column are deliberately\n * dropped: {@link splitTrailingLineSpec} parses them, and a start line is all\n * the editor has anywhere to put a cursor.\n *\n * `base` is where an address-relative path is resolved, and it must be the\n * base the ADDRESS was built with — the session's stored header cwd, see\n * `src/client/address-base.ts` — never the tab body's worktree root. Without\n * it the seed stays relative and every downstream reader (the viewer's\n * `fs.read`, the editor, the directory watch) re-bases it on the ACTIVE\n * worktree: a chat link to `<repo>/frontend/.worktrees/wt/a.md` arrives as\n * `frontend/.worktrees/wt/a.md` and is joined onto the worktree root a second\n * time (#947), or silently reads the same-named file of another checkout\n * (#950). Omitted (a caller with no session context) keeps the historical\n * relative seed.\n * @param info - the native tab record the body is drawing.\n * @param base - the address's own base, when the caller knows it.\n * @returns the seed, or `undefined` when the tab is not a file address.\n */\nexport function fileParamsOf(info: NativeTabInfo, base?: string): NativeTabParams | undefined {\n  const address = parseFileAddress(info.tab.contentId)\n  if (address === undefined) return undefined\n  // Resolve BEFORE the trailing line spec is split off: the spec belongs to\n  // the file name, and a base can only be prepended to the path.\n  const path = base === undefined ? address.path : resolveAddressPath(base, address.path)\n  const spec = splitTrailingLineSpec(path)\n  if (spec === undefined) return { path }\n  return { path: spec.path, title: baseName(spec.path), line: spec.line }\n}\n\n/**\n * Run one registration disposer, reporting a failure instead of propagating\n * it: releasing a registration must never mask the error being handled, and\n * one broken entry must not leave the others registered.\n *\n * A release failure is logged, NOT routed through `reportFailure` (the visible\n * diagnostic strip), on purpose: both callers run while the surface is being\n * taken down — the drop loop and the seat teardown — where a strip would just\n * be noise, and an id that really stays taken cannot hide anyway: the next\n * registration attempt for it goes through the strip as\n * `register … error: … already registered`.\n * @param dispose - the disposer to run.\n * @param what - the registration's name, for the log line.\n */\nfunction disposeSafely(dispose: () => void, what: string): void {\n  try {\n    dispose()\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`[dsh-better-sidebar] ${what} release failed:`, error)\n  }\n}\n\n/** Everything the registrations need. */\nexport interface NativeSurfaceDeps {\n  readonly ctx: Context\n  readonly store: SidebarStore\n  readonly service: BetterSidebarService\n  /** The shared native tab record registry (the surface writes it too). */\n  readonly records: NativeTabRecords\n  /**\n   * The live catalog of host guide cards. When present, the plugin replaces\n   * the shipped guide page with its own start page; omitted keeps the host's\n   * guide untouched (the unit harnesses use this to exercise the original\n   * surface without mounting the start page).\n   */\n  readonly guideCatalog?: NativeGuideCatalog\n  /**\n   * The activation's optional dsh-context diagnostics controller (see\n   * ../context-diagnostics.ts). Forwarded into the tab bodies' injected bag,\n   * because a native body renders in the HOST's React tree and cannot read the\n   * plugin shell's provider. Omitted = the bodies render without the\n   * diagnostics entry points.\n   */\n  readonly diagnostics?: ContextDiagnostics\n  /**\n   * Report a tab-type registration failure (phase label + cause).\n   *\n   * `ctx.inject`'s callback body and the registry's own subscriber callbacks\n   * run OUTSIDE this module's control flow, so a throw from\n   * `sidebarRightTabs.register` is swallowed by cordis and the whole native\n   * surface stays empty with no symptom beyond a missing guide. Reporting\n   * through the client's diagnostic strip (index.tsx `fail`) turns a silent\n   * contract break into a visible one — the failure mode observed when DSH\n   * 0.1.6-alpha.2 made `SidebarRightGuideEntry.id` required.\n   */\n  readonly reportFailure?: (phase: string, error: unknown) => void\n}\n\n/**\n * Register the plugin's tabs into the native right Sidebar and keep them in\n * step with the plugin's own registry and settings.\n * @param deps - client context, the plugin store/service, and the records.\n * @returns a disposer unregistering everything.\n */\nexport function registerNativeSurface(deps: NativeSurfaceDeps): () => void {\n  const { ctx, store, service, records, reportFailure, diagnostics, guideCatalog } = deps\n  // Bind the store BEFORE any body can render: the per-session state is the\n  // authority for the explorer's expansion set, so the native surface and the\n  // workbench share one set per session and a closed tab cannot drop it.\n  // (Restored after the v0.22.1 merge: main's branch rewrote this function\n  // without the call, and taking that file wholesale silently disabled every\n  // folder toggle — the records then have no store to read from or write to,\n  // so `toggleExpanded` returns without touching anything. Only the real-host\n  // lane could see it; the jsdom specs bind the records themselves.)\n  records.attachStore(store)\n  // Wait for the tab-type REGISTRY (a service), not for the slot declaration:\n  // the native seat declares `sidebar.right.pane.tab` BEFORE it provides\n  // `sidebarRightTabs`, so a declaration-triggered registration reads the\n  // service as missing and — because the declaration never collapses —\n  // registers nothing, permanently. Observed on a real profile: the\n  // declaration callback fired with both `sidebarRight` and\n  // `sidebarRightTabs` undefined, and the registry appeared a moment later.\n  // `ctx.inject` re-runs this body whenever the service appears/reappears,\n  // which is the lifecycle the registrations need.\n  const seat = ctx.inject(['sidebarRightTabs', 'sidebarRight'], (injected) => {\n    const tabs = injected.get('sidebarRightTabs')\n    if (tabs === undefined) return\n    const right = injected.get('sidebarRight') as (ISidebarRight & { registerCloseHandler(kind: string, handler: SidebarRightCloseHandler): () => void }) | undefined\n    const live = new Map<string, Registration>()\n\n    // The host runs this hook before removing a record (the strip's ×, its\n    // context menu, `page.close`, and a `replaceTab`). Flush the throttled\n    // draft here so the keystrokes of the last second survive the body's\n    // unmount; the hook is a synchronous cleanup, not a veto, so it cannot\n    // ask first (see editor-draft-backup.ts).\n    let disposeClose: (() => void) | undefined\n    if (typeof right?.registerCloseHandler === 'function') {\n      try {\n        disposeClose = right.registerCloseHandler(EDITOR_KIND, () => { flushDraftBackups() })\n      } catch (error) {\n        reportFailure?.('register editor close handler', error)\n      }\n    }\n\n    // The start page: replace the host guide body with the plugin's own grid.\n    // Its lifetime follows the `guideTakeover` preference, so turning the\n    // switch off unregisters the chain entry and the shipped guide resumes.\n    let disposeGuide: (() => void) | undefined\n    const syncGuide = (): void => {\n      if (guideCatalog === undefined) return\n      if (store.getPrefs().guideTakeover === false) {\n        if (disposeGuide !== undefined) {\n          disposeSafely(disposeGuide, 'the start-page guide takeover')\n          disposeGuide = undefined\n        }\n        return\n      }\n      if (disposeGuide !== undefined) return\n      const catalog = guideCatalog\n      try {\n        disposeGuide = ctx.slots.inject('sidebar.right.tab.guide', () => {\n          try {\n            return ctx.slots.register({\n              name: 'sidebar.right.tab.guide',\n              // Always elect: the shipped guide is the fallback we replace.\n              select: () => ({}),\n              inject: (sessionId: string) => {\n                const scope = typeof sessionId === 'string' && sessionId !== ''\n                  ? sessionId\n                  : mountedSessionId(ctx)\n                const terminals = webTerminals(ctx)\n                const navigation = ctx.get('pluginNavigation')\n                const workspace = ctx.get('uiWorkspace')\n                const onBrowsePlugins = typeof navigation?.openList === 'function'\n                  ? () => { navigation.openList!() }\n                  : undefined\n                const onCreatePlugin = typeof workspace?.startSession === 'function'\n                  ? () => {\n                    workspace.startSession!(undefined, {\n                      agentPreset: 'cordis',\n                      prompt: t('guideCreatePrompt'),\n                      whenDraftExists: 'append',\n                    })\n                  }\n                  : undefined\n                const shellMenu = scope !== undefined\n                  && terminals?.launchShells !== undefined\n                  && terminals?.selectShell !== undefined\n                  ? {\n                    // Call the methods on the SERVICE: the shell catalog reads\n                    // its own remote field, and a detached call throws\n                    // \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'remote')\".\n                    launchShells: (signal: AbortSignal) => terminals.launchShells(scope as SessionId, signal),\n                    selectShell: (path: string) => { terminals.selectShell!(path) },\n                  }\n                  : undefined\n                return {\n                  catalog,\n                  store,\n                  service,\n                  ...(shellMenu === undefined ? {} : { shellMenu }),\n                  ...(onBrowsePlugins === undefined ? {} : { onBrowsePlugins }),\n                  ...(onCreatePlugin === undefined ? {} : { onCreatePlugin }),\n                }\n              },\n            }, NativeGuide)\n          } catch (error) {\n            reportFailure?.('register start page', error)\n            return () => {}\n          }\n        })\n      } catch (error) {\n        reportFailure?.('register start page', error)\n      }\n    }\n\n    const fileSessionIdOf = (info: NativeTabInfo): string | undefined => {\n      const address = parseFileAddress(info.tab.contentId)\n      return address !== undefined && address.scope === 'session' ? address.sessionId : undefined\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Register the body + chip-title slots for one native implementation id.\n     *\n     * A slot registration can fail long after the TYPE registration succeeded\n     * (`ctx.effect` on a context that is already inactive, i.e. during a\n     * plugin reload/disposal), so the disposers are collected as they are\n     * handed out and the partial set is released on the way out: the caller\n     * must be able to roll its type registration back WITHOUT losing track of\n     * a slot that did register.\n     */\n    const registerSlots = (\n      id: string,\n      injected: Omit<NativeBodyInjected, 'sessionId'>,\n      params: Pick<NativeBodyInjected, 'paramsOf' | 'sessionIdOf'>,\n    ): Array<() => void> => {\n      // Collected AS THEY ARE HANDED OUT: a slot registration can fail long\n      // after the TYPE registration succeeded (a plugin reload makes\n      // `ctx.slots.inject` throw on the now-inactive context), and the caller\n      // must then be able to release the type again WITHOUT losing track of a\n      // slot that did register.\n      const disposers: Array<() => void> = []\n      try {\n        disposers.push(ctx.slots.inject('sidebar.right.pane.tab', () => ctx.slots.register({\n          name: 'sidebar.right.pane.tab',\n          key: id,\n          // The diagnostics controller rides the SAME injected bag every body\n          // already receives (a native body renders in the host's tree, so the\n          // plugin shell's provider is out of reach); the adapter turns it into\n          // the provider around the body it draws.\n          inject: (sessionId: string) => ({ ...injected, ...params, sessionId, ...(diagnostics === undefined ? {} : { diagnostics }) }),\n        }, NativeTabBody)))\n        disposers.push(ctx.slots.inject('sidebar.right.pane.tab.title', () => ctx.slots.register({\n          name: 'sidebar.right.pane.tab.title',\n          key: id,\n          // The chip draws a FILE tab's own glyph, so it needs the same\n          // address-derived seed the body gets: a file tab's address names the\n          // file it shows, and the chip must be able to draw it BEFORE — and\n          // without — the plugin-side record, which exists only after the body\n          // has rendered (and is gone again once the body unmounts).\n          // The chip is also drawn per session and BEFORE the body, so it needs\n          // its own session id: every session's tabs live in one registry, and\n          // a chip that guessed the session would show another one's title.\n          inject: (sessionId: string) => ({\n            records,\n            service,\n            descriptorId: injected.descriptorId,\n            sessionId,\n            ...(params.paramsOf === undefined ? {} : { paramsOf: params.paramsOf }),\n          }),\n        }, NativeTabTitle)))\n      } catch (error) {\n        for (const dispose of disposers) disposeSafely(dispose, `native tab slot \"${id}\"`)\n        throw error\n      }\n      return disposers\n    }\n\n    /** One descriptor's native type + body + title, as one disposable. */\n    const registerDescriptor = (descriptor: TabDescriptor): (() => void) => {\n      const id = nativeId(descriptor.id)\n      const isEditor = descriptor.id === EDITOR_KIND\n      const icon = descriptor.icon\n      const disposeType = tabs.register({\n        id,\n        kind: descriptor.id,\n        // 0.1.7: the host keeps a visited body MOUNTED through hiding,\n        // tab selection and Session switches, so the plugin's own React state\n        // (records, tree expansion, scroll, unsaved drafts) survives without\n        // the adapter faking it.\n        keepMounted: true,\n        ...(isEditor\n          ? {\n            patterns: ['dsh-resource://file/**'],\n            canOpen: (address: string) => {\n              const file = parseFileAddress(address)\n              // A non-file address, or one of the formats the built-in\n              // previews own, leaves the address to DSH's own `text` type.\n              return file !== undefined && !hostOwnedPath(file.path)\n            },\n          }\n          : {}),\n        // An external implementation outranks the product's own viewers, which\n        // is what lets the plugin's editor take over file addresses.\n        priority: 'extension',\n        // A resource tab is titled by the file it shows; a page tab keeps the\n        // descriptor's own title.\n        title: (address: string) => (isEditor ? fileTitleOf(address) ?? titleOf(descriptor) : titleOf(descriptor)),\n        // No guide entry for the editor: its page identity is the `files`\n        // kind takeover below (same view, same title), so listing both would\n        // offer the reader two identical \"Files\" rows. The type itself stays\n        // registered as the file RESOURCE viewer.\n        ...(descriptor.hidden === true || isEditor\n          ? {}\n          : {\n            guide: [{\n              // DSH 0.1.6-alpha.2 made `id` REQUIRED and unique per provider\n              // (a duplicate throws `sidebarRight: duplicate guide entry id`).\n              // The descriptor id is already unique per implementation, which\n              // is exactly the uniqueness the registry asks for.\n              id: descriptor.id,\n              order: descriptor.order ?? 100,\n              title: () => titleOf(descriptor),\n              ...guideDescriptionOf(descriptor),\n              ...guideIconOf(icon),\n            }],\n          }),\n      })\n      // The type is in the host's registry the moment `tabs.register`\n      // returns; a slot failure must release it here, or the id stays taken\n      // for the rest of the page's life (the host refuses a second\n      // registration of the same id) and the tab kind renders the host's\n      // \"nothing can view this\" face forever.\n      let slots: Array<() => void>\n      try {\n        slots = registerSlots(\n          id,\n          { ctx, store, service, records, descriptorId: descriptor.id },\n          isEditor\n            ? {\n              // The address's own session, not the seat's: a file address\n              // carries the session whose workspace resolves its path.\n              paramsOf: (info: NativeTabInfo) => fileParamsOf(info, addressBaseOf(ctx, fileSessionIdOf(info))),\n              sessionIdOf: fileSessionIdOf,\n            }\n            : {},\n        )\n      } catch (error) {\n        disposeSafely(disposeType, `native tab type \"${id}\"`)\n        throw error\n      }\n      return () => {\n        for (const dispose of slots.reverse()) disposeSafely(dispose, `native tab slot \"${id}\"`)\n        disposeSafely(disposeType, `native tab type \"${id}\"`)\n      }\n    }\n\n    /** One `files`-kind takeover: the plugin's explorer under the built-in kind. */\n    const registerFilesKind = (editor: TabDescriptor | undefined): (() => void) => {\n      const id = 'dsh-better-sidebar:files'\n      const disposeType = tabs.register({\n        id,\n        kind: FILES_KIND,\n        keepMounted: true,\n        priority: 'extension',\n        title: () => t('files'),\n        guide: [{\n          // Required and unique per provider since DSH 0.1.6-alpha.2. This\n          // takeover is its own implementation id, so its guide row takes\n          // that same id.\n          id: 'files',\n          order: 10,\n          title: () => t('files'),\n          // The takeover IS the editor descriptor's page, so it carries the\n          // editor's glyph AND guide line: without them the \"Files\" row is\n          // the only guide entry with a blank icon slot and no description.\n          ...guideDescriptionOf(editor),\n          ...guideIconOf(editor?.icon),\n        }],\n      })\n      let slots: Array<() => void>\n      try {\n        slots = registerSlots(id, { ctx, store, service, records, descriptorId: EDITOR_KIND }, {})\n      } catch (error) {\n        disposeSafely(disposeType, `native tab type \"${id}\"`)\n        throw error\n      }\n      return () => {\n        for (const dispose of slots.reverse()) disposeSafely(dispose, `native tab slot \"${id}\"`)\n        disposeSafely(disposeType, `native tab type \"${id}\"`)\n      }\n    }\n\n    /** Bring the live registrations in line with the registry + the settings. */\n    const sync = (): void => {\n      syncGuide()\n      const wanted = new Map<string, () => () => void>()\n      for (const descriptor of nativeTabDescriptors(service)) {\n        wanted.set(descriptor.id, () => registerDescriptor(descriptor))\n      }\n      for (const [descriptorId, registration] of live) {\n        // `files` is this module's OWN takeover, never a descriptor (`wanted`\n        // only ever holds descriptor ids): its lifetime belongs to the\n        // editor-type switch below. Disposing it here on EVERY notification\n        // (any prefs/state pulse, a Session switch included) re-mounted the\n        // explorer body and lost the tree's own component state — and a\n        // re-registration attempted on an already-inactive context (a plugin\n        // reload) left the type registered with nobody holding its disposer,\n        // so the same id could never be registered again for the rest of the\n        // page's life.\n        if (descriptorId === FILES_KIND || wanted.has(descriptorId)) continue\n        disposeSafely(() => registration.dispose(), `native tab type \"${descriptorId}\"`)\n        live.delete(descriptorId)\n      }\n      for (const [descriptorId, create] of wanted) {\n        if (live.has(descriptorId)) continue\n        // One descriptor must not take the rest of the surface down with it:\n        // report and continue so the remaining types still register. `create`\n        // has already released whatever it managed to install.\n        try {\n          live.set(descriptorId, { dispose: create() })\n        } catch (error) {\n          reportFailure?.(`register ${descriptorId}`, error)\n        }\n      }\n      // The built-in files kind follows the editor type's switch: with the\n      // editor disabled the plugin has no explorer to put there.\n      const wantsFiles = service.isTabEnabled(EDITOR_KIND)\n      const hasFiles = live.has(FILES_KIND)\n      if (wantsFiles && !hasFiles) {\n        try {\n          live.set(FILES_KIND, { dispose: registerFilesKind(service.getTab(EDITOR_KIND)) })\n        } catch (error) {\n          reportFailure?.(`register ${FILES_KIND}`, error)\n        }\n      }\n      if (!wantsFiles && hasFiles) {\n        const takeover = live.get(FILES_KIND)\n        live.delete(FILES_KIND)\n        if (takeover !== undefined) disposeSafely(() => takeover.dispose(), 'the native \"files\" takeover')\n      }\n    }\n\n    const disposeSubscriptions = [service.subscribe(sync), store.subscribe(sync)]\n    sync()\n    return () => {\n      for (const registration of live.values()) {\n        disposeSafely(() => registration.dispose(), 'a native tab registration')\n      }\n      live.clear()\n      for (const dispose of disposeSubscriptions.reverse()) disposeSafely(dispose, 'a native tab subscription')\n      if (disposeClose !== undefined) disposeSafely(disposeClose, 'the editor close handler')\n      if (disposeGuide !== undefined) disposeSafely(disposeGuide, 'the start-page guide takeover')\n    }\n  })\n  return () => {\n    void seat.dispose()\n  }\n}\n\nexport type { NativeTabRecords }\n","/**\n * The bottom workbench's expand/collapse control, registered into DSH's\n * session header utilities list (`conversation.session.header.utilities`).\n *\n * DSH 0.1.5 draws its own right-Sidebar expand button in the header's corner\n * slot (`conversation.session.header.corner`, a SINGLE slot owned by the\n * native sidebar package), so the plugin cannot take that seat. The utilities\n * list sits immediately left of it — the same row as the host's \"Session\n * log\" capsule — which is where a dock toggle belongs: in flow, so it never\n * overlaps host chrome and needs no absolute positioning or measurement.\n *\n * Registration goes through `slots.inject` because the declaration may not be\n * on the ledger yet at plugin activation (the ui-conversation parent entry\n * declares it); the callback re-runs if the declaration collapses and is\n * re-declared. `order: 10` places the button after the host's own utilities.\n */\nimport type { Context } from '../../context-types.ts'\nimport type { SidebarStore } from '../state.ts'\nimport { BottomDockToggle } from '../Sidebar.tsx'\n\n/** Register the header toggle; returns the disposer. */\nexport function registerBottomToggle(ctx: Context, store: SidebarStore): () => void {\n  return ctx.slots.inject('conversation.session.header.utilities', () => ctx.slots.register({\n    name: 'conversation.session.header.utilities',\n    id: 'dsh-better-sidebar:bottom-toggle',\n    order: 10,\n    registrant: 'dsh-better-sidebar',\n  }, () => <BottomDockToggle store={store} />))\n}\n","/** Adapt DSH's terminal factory to the slot-hosted Better Sidebar workbench. */\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport { PluginArtworkTerminal } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives'\nimport type { TerminalSurfaceInputProps } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-sidebar-terminal/client'\nimport { SessionId } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-session/types'\nimport type { Context } from '../../context-types.ts'\nimport type { BetterSidebarService, TabComponentProps } from '../service.ts'\nimport { allLeaves, type SidebarStore } from '../state.ts'\nimport { t } from '../locales.ts'\n\ntype TerminalSessionId = TerminalSurfaceInputProps['sessionId']\n\ninterface TerminalControllerFace {\n  close(sessionId: TerminalSessionId, key: string, contentId: string): void\n  retainTab(tab: { sessionId: TerminalSessionId; tabId: string; contentId: string }): () => void\n}\n\nfunction contentIdOf(sessionId: string, tabId: string): string {\n  return `better-sidebar:${sessionId}:${tabId}`\n}\n\nfunction terminalController(ctx: Context): TerminalControllerFace | undefined {\n  return ctx.get('webTerminals') as TerminalControllerFace | undefined\n}\n\n/** Register the workbench terminal tab and retain every cached Session occurrence. */\nexport function registerWorkbenchTerminal(ctx: Context, store: SidebarStore, service: BetterSidebarService): () => void {\n  const component = ({ scope, tab, visible, renderFactorySlot }: TabComponentProps): ReactNode => {\n    if (renderFactorySlot === undefined) return null\n    const replace = (): void => {\n      service.closeTab(tab.id, scope)\n      service.openTab({ type: 'terminal' }, scope)\n    }\n    const input: TerminalSurfaceInputProps = {\n      sessionId: SessionId(scope.sessionId),\n      tabId: tab.id,\n      contentId: contentIdOf(scope.sessionId, tab.id),\n      visible,\n      replace,\n    }\n    return renderFactorySlot('terminal.surface', input)\n  }\n  const disposeDescriptor = service.registerTab({\n    id: 'terminal',\n    title: () => t('terminal'),\n    description: () => t('guideDescTerminal'),\n    icon: size => <PluginArtworkTerminal size={size} />,\n    order: 40,\n    native: false,\n    available: () => terminalController(ctx) !== undefined,\n    createTab: () => ({\n      tab: {\n        id: `terminal:${crypto.randomUUID()}`,\n        type: 'terminal',\n        title: t('terminal'),\n      },\n    }),\n    onClose: (tab, scope) => {\n      terminalController(ctx)?.close(SessionId(scope.sessionId), tab.id, contentIdOf(scope.sessionId, tab.id))\n    },\n    component,\n  })\n  const seat = ctx.inject(['webTerminals'], () => {\n    const terminals = terminalController(ctx)\n    if (terminals === undefined) return\n    const holds = new Map<string, () => void>()\n    const syncHolds = (): void => {\n      const wanted = new Set<string>()\n      for (const [sessionId, state] of store.getSessionStates()) {\n        for (const leaf of allLeaves(state.bottomSplits)) {\n          for (const tab of leaf.tabs) {\n            if (tab.type !== 'terminal') continue\n            const contentId = contentIdOf(sessionId, tab.id)\n            wanted.add(contentId)\n            if (!holds.has(contentId)) {\n              holds.set(contentId, terminals.retainTab({ sessionId: SessionId(sessionId), tabId: tab.id, contentId }))\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n      for (const [contentId, release] of holds) {\n        if (wanted.has(contentId)) continue\n        release()\n        holds.delete(contentId)\n      }\n    }\n    const unsubscribe = store.subscribe(syncHolds)\n    syncHolds()\n    return () => {\n      unsubscribe()\n      for (const release of holds.values()) release()\n      holds.clear()\n    }\n  })\n  return () => {\n    void seat.dispose()\n    disposeDescriptor()\n  }\n}\n","/** Open HTTP(S) destinations through the desktop shell or an ordinary browser tab. */\nconst DESKTOP_EXTERNAL_LINK_CHANNEL = 'yourbuddy.desktop.external-link'\nconst DESKTOP_EXTERNAL_LINK_VERSION = 1\nconst MAX_EXTERNAL_URL_LENGTH = 4096\nlet externalLinkSequence = 0\n\n/**\n * Normalize an HTTP(S) destination accepted by the desktop shell.\n * @param value - Candidate absolute URL.\n * @returns The normalized URL, or undefined when the value is unsupported.\n */\nexport function resolveExternalHttpUrl(value: string): string | undefined {\n  if (value.length === 0 || value.length > MAX_EXTERNAL_URL_LENGTH) return void 0\n  try {\n    const url = new URL(value)\n    if (url.protocol !== 'http:' && url.protocol !== 'https:'\n      || url.hostname === ''\n      || url.username !== ''\n      || url.password !== ''\n      || url.href.length > MAX_EXTERNAL_URL_LENGTH) return void 0\n    return url.href\n  } catch {\n    return\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Dispatch an HTTP(S) destination without navigating the workbench.\n * @param value - Candidate absolute URL.\n * @returns True when the URL was sent to the desktop shell or browser API.\n */\nexport function openExternalHttpUrl(value: string): boolean {\n  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return false\n  const url = resolveExternalHttpUrl(value)\n  if (url === void 0) return false\n  if (window.parent !== window) {\n    externalLinkSequence += 1\n    window.parent.postMessage({\n      channel: DESKTOP_EXTERNAL_LINK_CHANNEL,\n      version: DESKTOP_EXTERNAL_LINK_VERSION,\n      type: 'open-request',\n      requestId: `${Date.now()}_${externalLinkSequence}`,\n      url\n    }, '*')\n    return true\n  }\n  const opened = window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer')\n  if (opened !== null) opened.opener = null\n  return true\n}\n","/**\n * External-link interception: clicking an http(s) link that a REGISTERED tab\n * type CLAIMS through `urlTarget` opens that type in the sidebar. Everything\n * else is left alone — the plugin never `preventDefault`s a link it cannot\n * serve, because the destination of a chat link is not the plugin's call:\n * since DSH 0.1.7 the host's `ui-chat` `openExternalLink` applies the user's\n * `linkOpening` setting and the host's own browser tab (a kind the Web\n * profile disables), and inside plugin-drawn markdown (sidechat\n * transcripts, editor previews, HTML previews, diff panes) the anchor's own\n * default (`window.open`) applies.\n *\n * A Ctrl/Cmd/Shift/Alt-modified click always bypasses the takeover so the\n * user can still force a real browser tab.\n *\n * Only the GUI's OWN document is watched — links inside a sandboxed iframe\n * live in another document and never bubble here (and their clicks must keep\n * working inside the sidebar).\n */\n\nimport { openExternalHttpUrl } from './desktop-external-links.ts'\n\n/** `new URL(value)`, or null for an unparsable href. */\nfunction parseUrl(value: string): URL | null {\n  try {\n    return new URL(value)\n  } catch {\n    return null\n  }\n}\n\n/** The pure decision: the URL a click may hand to the sidebar, or null to let\n *  the click fall through. Extracted so the policy is unit-testable without a\n *  DOM. `anchorHref` must be the ABSOLUTE href (`<a>.href` already is).\n *  The protocol/same-origin policy lives HERE; whether some enabled tab type\n *  actually claims the URL is the caller's `takeoverEnabled` callback. */\nexport function shouldInterceptLink(anchorHref: string, selfOrigin: string): string | null {\n  const url = parseUrl(anchorHref)\n  if (url === null) return null\n  if (url.protocol !== 'http:' && url.protocol !== 'https:') return null\n  // Same-origin links are GUI-internal navigation (settings pages, tool\n  // docs) — never routed into the sidebar.\n  try {\n    if (url.origin === new URL(selfOrigin).origin) return null\n  } catch {\n    // Unparsable selfOrigin (never in practice): intercept defensively.\n  }\n  return url.href\n}\n\n/** Whether a left-click may be taken over (unmodified left click only). */\nexport function isPlainLeftClick(event: { button: number; metaKey: boolean; ctrlKey: boolean; shiftKey: boolean; altKey: boolean }): boolean {\n  return event.button === 0 && !event.metaKey && !event.ctrlKey && !event.shiftKey && !event.altKey\n}\n\n/**\n * The caller-side gate: take a link over only when the sidebar is not\n * suspended AND some enabled tab type claims the URL. An unclaimed link is\n * the host's to route (its `openExternalLink` / the anchor's own default).\n */\nexport function shouldTakeOverLink(url: URL, opts: {\n  /** Another panel provider owns the right column — the sidebar must not act. */\n  suspended: boolean\n  /** The tab type claiming this URL through `urlTarget` (enabled tabs only). */\n  resolveTarget: (url: URL) => string | undefined\n}): boolean {\n  if (opts.suspended) return false\n  return opts.resolveTarget(url) !== undefined\n}\n\n/**\n * Whether a claimed type is still on offer at OPEN time: registered in the\n * tab registry AND not switched off in the settings. The claim (gate) and the\n * open are two separate turns of the event loop, so the type may disappear in\n * between — a plugin unloaded, the user disabled it, the registry reset.\n */\nexport function isTargetAvailable(\n  type: string,\n  tabs: readonly { id: string }[],\n  tabsEnabled: Record<string, boolean>,\n): boolean {\n  return tabs.some(tab => tab.id === type && tabsEnabled[tab.id] !== false)\n}\n\n/**\n * Open an intercepted link: the sidebar tab when the claimed type is still\n * available, a real browser tab otherwise. The fallback is not decoration —\n * the plugin's own `openTab` silently ignores an unknown / disabled type\n * (service.ts returns early), so without it a taken-over click would do\n * nothing at all. Returns the path taken (tests assert the fallback).\n */\nexport function openInterceptedLink(url: string, deps: {\n  /** The tab type claiming this URL through `urlTarget` (enabled tabs only). */\n  resolveTarget: (url: URL) => string | undefined\n  /** Whether that type is still registered and enabled ({@link isTargetAvailable}). */\n  isAvailable: (type: string) => boolean\n  /** The plugin's own tab service (`ctx.get('betterSidebar')`), when attached. */\n  sidebar: { openTab: (seed: { type: string; url: string; title?: string }) => void } | undefined\n}): 'sidebar' | 'window' {\n  const parsed = parseUrl(url)\n  const type = parsed === null ? undefined : deps.resolveTarget(parsed)\n  if (parsed !== null && type !== undefined && deps.sidebar !== undefined && deps.isAvailable(type)) {\n    deps.sidebar.openTab({ type, url, title: parsed.hostname })\n    return 'sidebar'\n  }\n  // Nothing in the sidebar can serve this URL (unclaimed, the type is gone or\n  // switched off, or the plugin's service is detached): hand it to the real\n  // browser so the click is never a silent no-op. A click IS the user\n  // gesture, so the popup blocker lets this through.\n  openExternalHttpUrl(url)\n  return 'window'\n}\n\n/**\n * Register the document-level click capture that funnels CLAIMED external\n * links into the sidebar. Returns the disposer (HMR-safe).\n */\nexport function registerLinkInterception(opts: {\n  /** Whether the takeover may happen for THIS url (the caller's gate —\n   *  {@link shouldTakeOverLink}: not suspended and claimed by an enabled\n   *  tab type). */\n  takeoverEnabled: (url: URL) => boolean\n  /** Open the URL — the caller resolves the claimed type and falls back to a\n   *  real browser tab when it is gone ({@link openInterceptedLink}). */\n  openInSidebar: (url: string) => void\n  /** The GUI's own origin (window.location.origin at registration). */\n  selfOrigin: string\n}): () => void {\n  const onClick = (event: MouseEvent): void => {\n    if (!isPlainLeftClick(event)) return\n    if (event.defaultPrevented) return\n    const target = event.target\n    if (target === null || typeof (target as Element).closest !== 'function') return\n    const anchor = (target as Element).closest('a[href]') as HTMLAnchorElement | null\n    if (anchor === null) return\n    const url = shouldInterceptLink(anchor.href, opts.selfOrigin)\n    if (url === null) return\n    if (!opts.takeoverEnabled(new URL(url))) return\n    event.preventDefault()\n    opts.openInSidebar(url)\n  }\n  document.addEventListener('click', onClick, true)\n  return () => { document.removeEventListener('click', onClick, true) }\n}\n","/**\n * The quote chip: \"add to conversation\" on a viewer selection mints a\n * reference chip into the composer draft instead of pasting the fenced text\n * block. The chip reads as `引用 a.md L12-15`, clicking it re-opens the file in\n * the sidebar editor and lands on the quoted lines (with a temporary flash),\n * and sending serializes it back to the same fenced block the pre-chip insert\n * produced — the model sees identical text, byte for byte.\n *\n * Since #1052 the selection popup already inserts a chip through the host's\n * built-in `'reference'` source, whose `ref` IS the payload (the whole fenced\n * block). That chip is inert: the host marks it openable only with an\n * `appearance`, and a click would hand the raw fence to the file opener. What\n * this module adds is the much smaller, source-owned alternative:\n *\n * - The chip's `ref` is a short opaque id ({@link QuoteRecord.id}); the\n *   selection lives in this module's store.\n * - One input-trigger source (`ctx.inputTriggers`, DSH 0.2.1+) owns that\n *   source name: `openReference` answers the click (open the file at the\n *   quoted lines), `codec.serialize` answers send-time expansion. A source\n *   with a `codec` is mandatory for insert outcomes — the host REFUSES a send\n *   whose chip has no